const WORD_SRC = {"available (adj.)":[["leader-113-22","Will you be \u0001available\u0002 to go with me?",""],["leader-113-52","A: Do you have brochures in Spanish? B: No, sorry, they're only \u0001available\u0002 in English.","A:你們有西班牙文的簡介手冊嗎? B:抱歉,只有英文版。"]],"complimentary (adj.)":[["guide-115-17","Some hotels in Taiwan offer \u0001complimentary\u0002 nice breakfast. You could try asking the front desk if your stay at the hotel includes a free breakfast.","台灣有些飯店提供免費招待的美味早餐。你可以問櫃台,你的住宿是否含免費早餐。"],["leader-114-38","The hotel provided each guest with a voucher for a \u0001complimentary\u0002 breakfast.","飯店提供每位客人一張免費早餐的兌換券。"]],"reservation (n.)":[["leader-115-4","Peter: Judy, I hope our \u0001reservation\u0002 at the restaurant is confirmed. Judy: Don't worry, I received the confirmation email this morning.","Peter:Judy,希望我們餐廳的訂位已經確認了。 Judy:別擔心,我今早收到確認信了。"],["leader-115-31","When visiting museums and other attractions in Paris, even if you have purchased a museum pass, making a(n) \u0001reservation\u0002 is still required.","在巴黎參觀博物館等景點時,即使買了博物館通票,仍需要事先預約。"]],"departure (n.)":[["guide-115-60","Before \u0001departure\u0002, please check the airline's official website to confirm that your flight is operating normally.","出發前,請查看航空公司官方網站,確認你的航班正常運作。"],["leader-113-19","This is your captain speaking. We apologize for our late \u0001departure\u0002, but as is sometimes the case at San Francisco, the fog was too thick for taking off.","我是機長。我們為延遲起飛道歉,但如舊金山常有的情況,霧太濃無法起飛。"]],"fasten (v.)":[["leader-113-16","Passenger: Would you please show me how to \u0001fasten\u0002 the seat belt?",""],["guide-113-26","Ladies and Gentlemen, as we are encountering some turbulence, the cruising is not stable. Please return to your seat and \u0001fasten\u0002 your seatbelt.","各位女士先生,由於我們遇到一些亂流,飛行不太穩定。請回座並繫好安全帶。"]],"accommodation (n.)":[["guide-115-3","Top \u0001accommodations\u0002 can be booked up weeks or even months in advance, so it's best to plan ahead before travelling abroad.","頂級住宿可能提前數週甚至數月就被訂滿,所以出國前最好提早規劃。"],["guide-113-62","Hotels operated by chains normally provide \u0001accommodations\u0002 ranging from budget to luxurious ones. However, there are still many privately owned inns and hotels that provide much less expensive rooms and meals than chain hotels.","連鎖經營的飯店通常提供從平價到豪華不等的住宿。然而,仍有許多私人經營的旅館提供比連鎖飯店便宜許多的房間與餐點。"]],"customs (n.)":[["leader-115-15","John: Mary, do we need to fill anything out for the souvenirs we bought abroad? Mary: Yes, we need to complete the \u0001customs\u0002 declaration form at the airport for items that may be restricted or taxable.","John:Mary,我們在國外買的紀念品需要填什麼嗎? Mary:要,對於可能受限制或需課稅的物品,得在機場填海關申報單。"],["guide-115-12","If you are bringing animals, plants, or their products into the country, to avoid penalties, apply for quarantine at \u0001customs\u0002 or the Animal and Plant Health Inspection Agency upon entry.","若攜帶動物、植物或其產品入境,為免受罰,請於入境時在海關或動植物防疫檢疫署申請檢疫。"]],"declare (v.)":[["leader-115-27","If you have nothing to \u0001declare\u0002, simply walk through the Green Channel, stopping only if asked to do so by a customs agent.","如果你沒有任何東西要申報,就直接走綠線通道,除非海關人員要求你停下。"],["leader-114-45","Make sure to \u0001declare\u0002 any items you bought abroad.",""]],"destination (n.)":[["leader-115-70","While we are en route to our next \u0001destination\u0002, I will point out the beautiful beach and the famous golf course for your reference.","在我們前往下一個目的地的途中,我會為各位指出美麗的海灘和著名的高爾夫球場。"],["guide-115-48","Jiufen, a mountain village in New Taipei City, is a popular \u0001destination\u0002 for international travelers mainly because of its old street.","九份是新北市的山城,主要因其老街而成為國際旅客熱門景點。"]],"facilities (n.)":[["guide-115-39","In Taiwan, special rental places such as \"whole-house lodging\" can be found. You can rent a whole house just for your party and have access to your own private \u0001facilities\u0002.","在台灣可找到「整棟出租(包棟民宿)」這類特別的租宿。你可以只為自己的團體租下整棟房子,擁有使用自己專屬設施的權利。"],["leader-113-12","The receptionist of a hotel is responsible for politely completing the check-in procedure and introducing the \u0001facilities\u0002 and services the hotel provides.","飯店櫃台負責禮貌地完成入住手續,並介紹飯店提供的設施和服務。"]],"indigenous (adj.)":[["guide-115-18","Taiwanese \u0001indigenous\u0002 people often use natural materials in their everyday items, such as clothes, accessories, and tools. For example, the Atayal often make clothing from ramie.","台灣原住民常在日常用品(如衣物、飾品、工具)中使用天然材料。例如,泰雅族常用苧麻製衣。"],["guide-115-46","The \u0001indigenous\u0002 people of Alishan, the Tsou people, are comprised of nine major tribes, each holding their own celebrations every year from September to December jointly referred to as the famous \"Tsou Annual Festival\" of Alishan.","阿里山的原住民鄒族由九大部落組成,各部落每年 9 月至 12 月舉辦自己的慶典,合稱著名的阿里山「鄒族年度祭典」。"]],"itinerary (n.)":[["guide-113-35","When you come to Penghu, you may sign up for an island-hopping tour with everything from half-day to multi-day \u0001itineraries\u0002 available.","來澎湖時,你可以報名跳島之旅,從半日到多日的行程都有。"],["leader-112-38","Here is the \u0001itinerary\u0002 for my trip to Europe this coming summer. Do you have any suggestions?","這是我今夏歐洲之旅的行程表。你有什麼建議嗎?"]],"passport (n.)":[["leader-115-3","Before entering the country, each visitor must have a valid \u0001passport\u0002 ready for inspection.","入境前,每位旅客都必須備妥有效護照以供查驗。"],["guide-113-53","Passenger: Hi, I'd like to check in for my flight to New York, please. Check-in Agent: Of course, may I have your \u0001passport\u0002 and e-ticket, please?","旅客:你好,我想辦理飛往紐約的報到。 報到人員:當然,請給我你的護照和電子機票好嗎?"]],"prohibited (adj.)":[["leader-115-60","In many museums, touching the exhibited items is a behavior that is absolutely \u0001prohibited\u0002.","在許多博物館,觸摸展示品是絕對被禁止的行為。"],["leader-114-46","The security officer had to confiscate the \u0001prohibited\u0002 items from the passenger's luggage.","安檢人員必須從乘客行李中沒收違禁品。"]],"souvenir (n.)":[["leader-113-67","To buy \u0001souvenirs\u0002 at the local market, tourists often need to exchange their currency for the local money.","要在當地市場買紀念品,遊客常需把貨幣兌換成當地錢幣。"],["guide-113-76","While some people travel to see historic sights or hit the road in search of boutiques and \u0001souvenirs\u0002, more and more people are getting bit by the culinary travel bug.","",1]],"discount (n.)":[["leader-114-30","To bring more tourists to Taiwan, the government should offer attractive incentive like \u0001discounts\u0002 and special deals.","為了吸引更多遊客來台灣,政府應提供有吸引力的誘因,例如折扣和特別優惠。"],["leader-113-36","A Periodic Ticket allows an unlimited number of rides to and from designated stations at a bargain rate within the offer validity period. The \u0001discount\u0002 is calculated based on the full fares for Non-reserved Seats.","定期票在效期內,可於指定車站間無限次搭乘,享優惠費率。折扣依非劃位車廂的全票價計算。"]],"landmark (n.)":[["leader-115-48","On the city tour, the guide asked everyone to take a photo in front of the famous \u0001landmark\u0002 that represents the history of the area.","市區觀光時,導遊請大家在代表當地歷史的著名地標前拍照。"],["guide-115-61","The \"Yehliu Geopark\" is one of the most famous \u0001landmarks\u0002 of Taiwan.","「野柳地質公園」是台灣最著名的地標之一。"]],"luggage (n.)":[["leader-114-36","Ground Staff: Can you identify which one resembles your \u0001luggage\u0002? (Showing a card with various types of luggage.) Amy: Mine looks similar to Type D.","地勤:你能辨認出哪一個像你的行李嗎?(出示各種行李款式的卡片) Amy:我的很像 D 型。"],["guide-114-49","Make sure that your \u0001luggage\u0002 has successfully passed through X-ray inspection before you leave the check-in area.","離開報到區前,請確認你的行李已順利通過 X 光檢查。"]],"receipt (n.)":[["leader-113-41","Do you have your \u0001receipt\u0002?",""],["leader-112-62","A: Besides the discount, we can also keep the \u0001receipts\u0002 to get a VAT (value-added tax) refund at the airport. B: So great!","A:除了折扣,我們還能留著收據到機場辦加值稅退稅。 B:太棒了!"]],"refund (n.)":[["leader-112-62","A: Besides the discount, we can also keep the receipts to get a VAT (value-added tax) \u0001refund\u0002 at the airport. B: So great!","A:除了折扣,我們還能留著收據到機場辦加值稅退稅。 B:太棒了!"],["guide-112-46","If you are not completely satisfied with our product, you can return it for a full \u0001refund\u0002.","如果你對我們的產品不完全滿意,可以退貨並獲得全額退款。"]],"attraction (n.)":[["leader-115-38","The destination is a big city with countless tourist \u0001attractions\u0002; we plan to visit at least six or more of the most recommended ones.","這個目的地是個有無數觀光景點的大城市;我們計畫至少參觀六個以上最推薦的。"],["leader-115-66","Drawing many people's attention, Jurassic World: The Experience at Cloud Forest is one of the most recently added \u0001attractions\u0002 in Singapore.","吸引眾人目光的「侏羅紀世界:雲霧森林體驗」是新加坡最新增設的景點之一。"]],"bill (n.)":[["leader-115-61","Let me calculate your \u0001bill\u0002 for you. It all adds up to NT$15,000, Sir.","先生,我幫您算帳,全部加起來總共台幣 15,000 元。"],["leader-113-34","The answer to how much we should tip a waitress can be varied. Some people think 10 to 15% of your \u0001bill\u0002 is the proper amount.","我們該給服務生多少小費,答案不一。有些人認為帳單的 10–15% 是適當金額。"]],"brochure (n.)":[["leader-113-52","A: Do you have \u0001brochures\u0002 in Spanish? B: No, sorry, they're only available in English.","A:你們有西班牙文的簡介手冊嗎? B:抱歉,只有英文版。"],["guide-113-25","Here is a guidebook and some \u0001brochures\u0002 providing detailed information about the city and the city tours.",""]],"confirm (v.)":[["leader-115-4","Peter: Judy, I hope our reservation at the restaurant is \u0001confirmed\u0002. Judy: Don't worry, I received the confirmation email this morning.","Peter:Judy,希望我們餐廳的訂位已經確認了。 Judy:別擔心,我今早收到確認信了。"],["guide-115-60","Before departure, please check the airline's official website to \u0001confirm\u0002 that your flight is operating normally.","出發前,請查看航空公司官方網站,確認你的航班正常運作。"]],"declaration (n.)":[["leader-115-15","John: Mary, do we need to fill anything out for the souvenirs we bought abroad? Mary: Yes, we need to complete the customs \u0001declaration\u0002 form at the airport for items that may be restricted or taxable.","John:Mary,我們在國外買的紀念品需要填什麼嗎? Mary:要,對於可能受限制或需課稅的物品,得在機場填海關申報單。"],["leader-112-18","Passengers arriving in Taiwan must fill out a health \u0001declaration\u0002 form.","抵達台灣的旅客須填寫健康申報表。"]],"emergency (n.)":[["leader-115-65","Tourists on the plane were reminded how to use oxygen masks in case of \u0001emergency\u0002.","機上乘客被提醒如何在緊急情況下使用氧氣面罩。"],["leader-112-3","Flight attendant: Don't inflate your life jacket until you've left the plane in case of \u0001emergency\u0002.","空服員:緊急時,離開飛機前請勿為救生衣充氣。"]],"flight (n.)":[["leader-111-42","Customer: I would like to confirm my \u0001flight\u0002 from Taipei to Los Angeles. Airline agent: May I have your name and ticket number, please?","顧客:我想確認台北到洛杉磯的航班。 地勤:能給我你的姓名和票號嗎?"],["guide-111-45","Did Alex's \u0001flight\u0002 to Taipei depart on time?","Alex 飛台北的班機準時起飛了嗎?"]],"passenger (n.)":[["guide-115-44","A: Can I bring my pet along on the trip? B: No, to protect the rights and comfort of all \u0001passengers\u0002, pets are forbidden on board.","A:我可以帶寵物一起去嗎? B:不行,為保障所有乘客的權益與舒適,寵物禁止上車/機。"],["leader-112-18","\u0001Passengers\u0002 arriving in Taiwan must fill out a health declaration form.","抵達台灣的旅客須填寫健康申報表。"]],"prescription (n.)":[["guide-113-57","The pharmacy is where you can fill your \u0001prescriptions\u0002 and purchase over-the-counter medications and health-related products.","藥局是你可以領處方藥、購買成藥與健康相關產品的地方。"],["leader-112-23","Some \u0001prescription\u0002 medications are illegal in Taiwan. Authorities may jail or fine you if you have them.","有些處方藥在台灣是違法的。若攜帶,當局可能將你監禁或罰款。"]],"quarantine (n.)":[["guide-115-12","If you are bringing animals, plants, or their products into the country, to avoid penalties, apply for \u0001quarantine\u0002 at customs or the Animal and Plant Health Inspection Agency upon entry.","若攜帶動物、植物或其產品入境,為免受罰,請於入境時在海關或動植物防疫檢疫署申請檢疫。"],["leader-112-25","Effective from October 13, 2022, Taiwan has lifted the \u0001quarantine\u0002 requirement for all arrivals, so arriving travelers will no longer be required to quarantine.","自 2022 年 10 月 13 日起,台灣取消所有入境者的隔離要求,入境旅客不再須隔離。"]],"route (n.)":[["guide-115-22","The trail around Sun Moon Lake in Nantou is listed as one of the 10 best cycling \u0001routes\u0002 in the world by CNN.","南投日月潭的環湖步道被 CNN 列為全球十大最佳自行車路線之一。"],["leader-114-65","The new \u0001route\u0002 to the northern coast region creates more opportunities for tourists to enjoy all the spectacular view of the area.","通往北海岸地區的新路線,為遊客創造更多欣賞該區壯麗景色的機會。"]],"turbulence (n.)":[["guide-113-26","Ladies and Gentlemen, as we are encountering some \u0001turbulence\u0002, the cruising is not stable. Please return to your seat and fasten your seatbelt.","各位女士先生,由於我們遇到一些亂流,飛行不太穩定。請回座並繫好安全帶。"],["guide-112-11","You must remain seated while the fasten-seat-belt signals are illuminated during \u0001turbulence\u0002.","亂流期間,當繫安全帶指示燈亮起時,你必須保持坐好。"]],"abroad (adv.)":[["guide-112-13","Do I need to dial the international area code while making a call \u0001abroad\u0002?","打國際電話時,我需要撥國際區碼嗎?"],["guide-112-62","Before going \u0001abroad\u0002, you need to understand the current exchange rates and have some New Taiwan dollars converted into U.S. dollars.","出國前,你需要了解目前的匯率,並把一些新台幣兌換成美元。"]],"airport (n.)":[["leader-110-6","You need to be at the \u0001airport\u0002 by 10:00.",""],["leader-107-2","It is very kind of you to give me a ride to the \u0001airport\u0002.","你真好心載我去機場。"]],"belongings (n.)":[["guide-115-1","When you are in public places, be sure not to leave your personal \u0001belongings\u0002 unattended.","在公共場所,務必不要讓你的個人隨身物品無人看管。"],["leader-114-28","Make sure to purchase a strong and durable carry-on bag to ensure your \u0001belongings\u0002 are safe during travel.","務必買一個堅固耐用的隨身包,確保旅行時物品安全。"]],"capacity (n.)":[["leader-114-33","European airlines are increasing their \u0001capacity\u0002 as the expansion trend that began late last year continues.","隨著去年底開始的擴張趨勢持續,歐洲航空公司正在增加運能。"],["guide-114-72","Boosting the \u0001capacity\u0002 of the sector to attract, retain and develop a strong and sustainable workforce is a further area of ongoing focus.","",4]],"culinary (adj.)":[["guide-114-31","It is said that one of the great strengths of its \u0001culinary\u0002 landscape is its accessibility.",""],["guide-113-76","\u0001Culinary\u0002 tourism is one of the hottest trends in travel.","",1]],"exceed (v.)":[["guide-114-18","The medical assistive devices used by passengers may not \u0001exceed\u0002 125 cm in length, 90 cm in width, and 185 cm in height.","乘客使用的醫療輔助裝置不得超過長 125 公分、寬 90 公分、高 185 公分。"],["leader-112-27","Foreigners with a valid passport/travel document and whose stay in R.O.C does not \u0001exceed\u0002 a period of 183 days are eligible to apply for a tax refund.","持有效護照/旅行證件、且在台停留不超過 183 天的外國人,符合退稅資格。"]],"immigration (n.)":[["leader-115-32","Officers at \u0001immigration\u0002 check all passports and visas before travelers can enter the country.","入境查驗處的官員會查驗所有護照和簽證,旅客才能入境。"],["guide-114-40","\u0001Immigration\u0002 is the place where government officials check travelers to make sure they can legally get in or get out of the country.","證照查驗處是政府官員查驗旅客、確保他們能合法入境或出境的地方。"]],"infer (v.)":[["leader-115-73","Based on the information presented in this passage, what can be \u0001inferred\u0002?","根據本文資訊,可以推論出什麼?"],["guide-114-79","Which of the following can be \u0001inferred\u0002 from the passage?","根據本文,下列何者可以被推論出來?"]],"museum (n.)":[["leader-110-38","Technology allows people to go on virtual tours on their computers to see \u0001museums\u0002, world heritage sites, and other attractions before they plan a trip.","科技讓人能在電腦上進行虛擬導覽,在規劃旅程前先看博物館、世界遺產和其他景點。"],["leader-109-22","Ian needed to look at the map on his mobile phone several times because he didn't know the route to the \u0001museum\u0002.","Ian 得看好幾次手機地圖,因為他不知道去博物館的路線。"]],"purpose (n.)":[["leader-115-75","What can be described as the \u0001purpose\u0002 of this passage?","本文的寫作目的為何?"],["leader-113-69","What is the \u0001purpose\u0002 of your visit?",""]],"restriction (n.)":[["leader-114-12","Due to the \u0001restrictions\u0002 on the size of the carry-on luggage, it can be challenging to choose the ideal personal bag for flights.","由於隨身行李尺寸的限制,要選到理想的個人包包可能很有挑戰性。"],["leader-114-34","Passengers often get upset due to long lines and confusion about ticket \u0001restrictions\u0002 hidden in the small print of discounted fares.","乘客常因長長的隊伍,以及對折扣票價小字裡隱藏的票務限制感到困惑而不悅。"]],"spectacular (adj.)":[["leader-115-21","The \u0001spectacular\u0002 Northeast Coast is a popular tourist destination that serves both as a fascinating natural classroom and as an enchanting coastal playground.","壯觀的東北角海岸是熱門觀光勝地,既是迷人的天然教室,也是迷人的海岸遊樂場。"],["leader-114-65","The new route to the northern coast region creates more opportunities for tourists to enjoy all the \u0001spectacular\u0002 view of the area.","通往北海岸地區的新路線,為遊客創造更多欣賞該區壯麗景色的機會。"]],"sustainable (adj.)":[["guide-114-71","These strategies look to build on recent momentum to shift to more \u0001sustainable\u0002 models of tourism, to adapt to an increasingly dynamic environment and engage stakeholders around a common vision for the future of the sector.","",1],["leader-113-45","Ecological tourism encourages \u0001sustainable\u0002 travel, fostering appreciation for natural wonders while promoting conservation efforts crucial for preserving our planet's biodiversity.","生態旅遊鼓勵永續旅行,培養對自然奇景的欣賞,同時推動對保護地球生物多樣性至關重要的保育工作。"]],"treasure (n.)":[["guide-115-33","The Alishan Forest Railway is a \u0001treasure\u0002 of Taiwan. Every day, the train takes passengers on wonderful rides forward through different forest types.","阿里山森林鐵路是台灣的瑰寶。每天,火車載著旅客穿越不同森林類型,展開美妙的旅程。"],["guide-115-62","The National Palace Museum houses the world's largest collection of priceless Chinese art \u0001treasures\u0002.","故宮博物院收藏著全世界最大的無價中華藝術珍寶典藏。"]],"valid (adj.)":[["leader-115-3","Before entering the country, each visitor must have a \u0001valid\u0002 passport ready for inspection.","入境前,每位旅客都必須備妥有效護照以供查驗。"],["leader-112-27","Foreigners with a \u0001valid\u0002 passport/travel document and whose stay in R.O.C does not exceed a period of 183 days are eligible to apply for a tax refund.","持有效護照/旅行證件、且在台停留不超過 183 天的外國人,符合退稅資格。"]],"vendor (n.)":[["leader-115-7","Be ready for the warm-hearted \u0001vendors\u0002 on these streets; they are super friendly and always eager to persuade you to buy their items.","要有心理準備,這些街上有熱情的攤販;他們超友善,總是急著說服你買他們的東西。"],["leader-115-8","If you buy some souvenirs from local \u0001vendors\u0002 in Thailand, you should try to bargain for a good deal because the first price offered is usually much higher.","如果你在泰國向當地攤販買紀念品,應該試著殺價以爭取好價錢,因為對方開出的第一個價通常高很多。"]],"allowance (n.)":[["leader-112-43","Each passenger can have two pieces of checked baggage \u0001allowance\u0002 and one carry-on bag.","每位乘客可有兩件託運行李額度和一件隨身行李。"],["leader-112-46","If you carry more than the duty-free \u0001allowance\u0002, including a bottle of alcohol, the items will be confiscated.","若攜帶超過免稅額度(含一瓶酒),物品將被沒收。"]],"authentic (adj.)":[["leader-114-32","Tourists now seek more \u0001authentic\u0002 experiences involving real communities and people instead of simply following a tour guide's flag.","遊客現在尋求更道地的體驗,涉及真實的社區與人們,而不是單純跟著導遊的旗子走。"],["guide-113-76","Travel has been trending increasingly towards \u0001authentic\u0002 experiences.","",4]],"book (v.)":[["leader-113-7","As soon as your traveling date is fixed, you need to \u0001book\u0002 yourself a flight ticket and make your hotel reservations.","旅行日期一確定,你就得訂機票和訂飯店。"],["leader-112-50","A: Is it possible to \u0001book\u0002 an opera ticket and a local tour for me?",""]],"breathtaking (adj.)":[["leader-115-18","The magnificent waterfall is truly the most \u0001breathtaking\u0002 feature of this national park.","那壯麗的瀑布真是這座國家公園最令人屏息的特色。"],["guide-114-36","When in central Taiwan, railroad enthusiasts can plan a railway journey to Changhua Sector Garage. It has a round platform with 12 tracks that spread out like a fan—a \u0001breathtaking\u0002 sight!","在中台灣時,鐵道迷可以規劃一趟前往彰化扇形車庫的鐵道之旅。那裡有座圓形月台、12 條軌道如扇形展開——令人驚豔!"]],"concierge (n.)":[["leader-112-50","The \u0001concierge\u0002 service in our hotel can help.",""],["guide-112-61","A \u0001concierge\u0002 is someone who is employed in a hotel to help guests arrange things, such as local tours, theatre tickets and restaurant reservations.","禮賓員是飯店雇用來協助客人安排事務(如當地旅遊、劇院票券和餐廳訂位)的人。"]],"cuisine (n.)":[["guide-114-26","Common ingredients of Taiwanese \u0001cuisine\u0002 are pork, seafood, rice, soy, and chicken.","台灣料理常見的食材有豬肉、海鮮、米、大豆和雞肉。"],["guide-112-31","A: How does Mexican \u0001cuisine\u0002 taste? B: It has a spicy and heavy flavor.","A:墨西哥菜嚐起來如何? B:它味道又辣又重。"]],"currency (n.)":[["leader-113-67","To buy souvenirs at the local market, tourists often need to exchange their \u0001currency\u0002 for the local money.","要在當地市場買紀念品,遊客常需把貨幣兌換成當地錢幣。"],["leader-112-47","Changing money at the airport is convenient to get local \u0001currency\u0002, but you may be charged some service fees.","在機場換錢方便取得當地貨幣,但可能被收手續費。"]],"destroy (v.)":[["leader-115-36","Littering in natural parks can \u0001destroy\u0002 the beauty tourists come to admire.","在自然公園亂丟垃圾會破壞遊客前來欣賞的美景。"],["leader-114-1","The Maui wildfire in Hawaii last year took 102 lives and \u0001destroyed\u0002 80% of the town of Lahaina.","夏威夷茂宜島去年的野火奪走 102 條人命,並摧毀了拉海納鎮 80% 的地區。"]],"dish (n.)":[["leader-115-5","If you plan to try some exotic \u0001dishes\u0002 when traveling to a different country, please do some research about what those dishes are.","如果你到不同國家想嘗試一些異國風味的菜,請先研究一下那些是什麼菜。"],["leader-113-13","There are also vegetarian \u0001dishes\u0002 on our à la carte menu.",""]],"domestic (adj.)":[["leader-112-63","Excuse me, could you show me how to make a \u0001domestic\u0002 long-distance call from San Diego to New York?","不好意思,能教我怎麼從聖地牙哥打國內長途電話到紐約嗎?"],["guide-112-25","To compensate for the loss of foreign tourists caused by COVID-19 restrictions, Taiwanese travel businesses have shifted gears towards \u0001domestic\u0002 trips.","為彌補 COVID-19 限制造成的外國遊客流失,台灣旅遊業者已轉換方向(改變策略)轉向國內旅遊。"]],"embassy (n.)":[["leader-112-70","A: What can I do if I lose my passport during the trip? B: You have to go to the \u0001embassy\u0002 to have a new one reissued.","A:旅途中護照弄丟了怎麼辦? B:你得去大使館補發一本新的。"],["leader-111-58","If a traveler loses his or her passport, he or she needs to find his or her country's \u0001embassy\u0002 to apply for a temporary passport.","若旅客遺失護照,須找到自己國家的大使館申請臨時護照。"]],"exhibition (n.)":[["guide-109-50","A: Do I need tickets for Taiwan Culinary \u0001Exhibition\u0002? B: It's free and open to the public.","A:台灣美食展需要門票嗎? B:免費且對大眾開放。"],["leader-108-76","The new \u0001exhibition\u0002 allows people to analyze why they love and hate certain foods.","",4]],"explore (v.)":[["leader-115-35","The city's urban center is quite compact and easy to \u0001explore\u0002 on foot or by bike.","這座城市的市中心相當緊湊,很適合步行或騎單車遊覽。"],["leader-114-50","Nancy: At least we can \u0001explore\u0002 the airport shops while we wait.",""]],"fare (n.)":[["leader-115-42","Passengers simply add value to a smart card and swipe it at the gate to enter. The \u0001fare\u0002 is automatically deducted.","乘客只要為智慧卡加值,在閘門刷卡進入,車資就會自動扣除。"],["leader-113-35","Do you know how much the \u0001fare\u0002 is?",""]],"guarantee (v.)":[["guide-112-49","The salespersons \u0001guaranteed\u0002 that their organic foods do not have preservatives.","售貨員保證他們的有機食品不含防腐劑。"],["leader-109-34","The agent in a car rental company \u0001guaranteed\u0002 that he would reserve a car for Nancy if she could pay a deposit to confirm her reservation.","租車公司的專員保證,只要 Nancy 付訂金確認,就會為她預留一輛車。"]],"heritage (n.)":[["guide-115-31","Longshan Temple, located in Wanhua, is one of Taipei's finest examples of Taiwan's architectural and historical \u0001heritage\u0002.","位於萬華的龍山寺,是台灣建築與歷史遺產的最佳範例之一。"],["leader-115-71","Tourism is often a primary source of income for many regions, especially those rich in natural beauty, historical importance, or cultural \u0001heritage\u0002.","",1]],"infrastructure (n.)":[["guide-115-76","That analysis factors in the cost of purchasing an electric car and outfitting it with autonomous technology, installing and using electric vehicle charging \u0001infrastructure\u0002, fleet maintenance, insurance, vehicle teleoperation and other costs.","",1],["guide-114-71","Tourism destinations and businesses need support to keep pace with rapid technological developments, while resources are also required to develop the transport and other \u0001infrastructure\u0002 needed to better manage tourism development.","",1]],"landscape (n.)":[["leader-115-78","What does the word \"fragmented\" in the phrase \"fragmented regulatory \u0001landscape\u0002\" most nearly mean?","在「fragmented regulatory landscape(破碎/各自為政的法規環境)」這個詞組中,\"fragmented\" 一字最接近的意思是?"],["guide-114-21","Taroko National Park is a popular destination for international travelers because of its spectacular \u0001landscapes\u0002.","太魯閣國家公園因其壯觀的景觀,成為國際旅客的熱門景點。"]],"maintenance (n.)":[["guide-113-64","I'll speak to the \u0001maintenance\u0002 department.",""],["leader-112-51","I will send a \u0001maintenance\u0002 staff up right away.",""]],"pilgrimage (n.)":[["guide-115-14","The Mazu \u0001pilgrimage\u0002 is one of the most noted folk religious festivals in Taiwan. People go on a journey to honor the goddess Mazu.","媽祖遶境進香是台灣最著名的民間宗教節慶之一。人們踏上旅程來敬奉媽祖女神。"],["guide-114-27","The Mazu \u0001pilgrimage\u0002, which lasts over a week and covers hundreds of kilometers, is one of Taiwan's religious festivals. It is like an enormous birthday celebration for the “Goddess of the Sea.”","媽祖遶境進香持續一週以上、綿延數百公里,是台灣的宗教節慶之一,就像為「海上女神」舉辦的盛大生日慶典。"]],"popular (adj.)":[["leader-112-40","Taiwan has become more and more \u0001popular\u0002 among foreign tourists because it is quite affordable and friendly.","台灣越來越受外國旅客歡迎,因為它相當物價實惠又友善。"],["leader-111-53","Many immigrants live in Australia, so ethnic food is very \u0001popular\u0002 here.","許多移民住在澳洲,所以異國(族裔)料理在這很受歡迎。"]],"rate (n.)":[["guide-113-5","Caller: How much are your single rooms? Front Desk Clerk: The \u0001rates\u0002 vary depending upon the season and type of single rooms.","來電者:你們的單人房多少錢? 櫃台:價格會依季節與單人房型而有所不同。"],["leader-111-20","International calls to mobile phones registered in another country are charged higher \u0001rates\u0002. The first zero of an international number must be deleted since it is a \"trunk prefix\" only for domestic calls within many countries.","打到在他國註冊的手機的國際電話會被收取較高費率。國際號碼開頭的 0 須刪去,因它是在許多國家只供國內電話使用的「長途字冠」。"]],"reserve (v.)":[["leader-112-14","Waiter: Good evening, Grand Restaurant, may I help you? Customer: I would like to \u0001reserve\u0002 a table for tonight.","服務生:晚安,Grand 餐廳,能為您服務嗎? 顧客:我想預訂今晚的位子。"],["leader-111-50","Tourist: I would like to \u0001reserve\u0002 a room for this weekend.",""]],"restricted (adj.)":[["leader-115-15","John: Mary, do we need to fill anything out for the souvenirs we bought abroad? Mary: Yes, we need to complete the customs declaration form at the airport for items that may be \u0001restricted\u0002 or taxable.","John:Mary,我們在國外買的紀念品需要填什麼嗎? Mary:要,對於可能受限制或需課稅的物品,得在機場填海關申報單。"],["guide-114-41","You must declare or dispose of any prohibited or \u0001restricted\u0002 goods before you reach customs.","抵達海關前,你必須申報或丟棄任何違禁或受限制的物品。"]],"shuttle (n.)":[["leader-114-68","There is a wide variety of hotels conveniently located near the airport and many of them offer hotel courtesy \u0001shuttles\u0002.","機場附近有各式各樣位置便利的飯店,許多提供免費接駁車。"],["leader-111-49","Many hotels in New York provide free airport \u0001shuttle\u0002 service. You could also take the subway if you are comfortable with public transportation.","紐約許多飯店提供免費機場接駁服務。若你習慣搭大眾運輸,也可搭地鐵。"]],"species (n.)":[["guide-113-15","The conservation of jungles and rainforests is critical to the survival of many \u0001species\u0002.","叢林與雨林的保育對許多物種的生存至關重要。"],["guide-111-26","The Formosan black bear is a \u0001species\u0002 indigenous to Taiwan and currently listed as “endangered” under Taiwan's Wildlife Conservation Act.","台灣黑熊是原生於台灣的物種,目前依《野生動物保育法》被列為「瀕危」。"]],"volcano (n.)":[["guide-115-40","The \u0001volcano\u0002 on the island has been unusually active over the past few days; many residents are afraid that it is going to erupt in no time.","島上的火山過去幾天異常活躍;許多居民擔心它很快就要噴發。"],["guide-114-24","Xiaoyoukeng, located in Yangmingshan National Park, is probably one of the best places to feel the pulsation of the \u0001volcano\u0002 under your feet.","位於陽明山國家公園的小油坑,大概是最能感受腳下火山脈動的地方之一。"]],"wheelchair (n.)":[["leader-112-67","My ankle was sprained, so walking was quite hard. I think I may need a \u0001wheelchair\u0002 for assistance at the airport.","我的腳踝扭傷了,走路很吃力。我想在機場可能需要輪椅協助。"],["leader-110-31","To provide a disabled-friendly lodging environment, the features of a guest room for people in a \u0001wheelchair\u0002 include lower cloth rails, an adjustable bed, a shower chair, and a raised toilet.","為提供身障友善的住宿環境,供輪椅使用者的客房設計特徵包括較低的掛桿、可調式床、淋浴椅和加高馬桶。"]],"accommodate (v.)":[["guide-113-16","Due to increased demand, the national park started issuing more permits for overnight camping to \u0001accommodate\u0002 more hikers.","由於需求增加,國家公園開始發放更多過夜露營許可證,以容納更多登山客。"],["guide-112-51","Designed by British architects, the hotel can \u0001accommodate\u0002 more than 700 people.","這家由英國建築師設計的飯店可容納超過 700 人。"]],"aircraft (n.)":[["leader-112-4","Please remain seated until the \"fasten seat belt\" sign is switched off and the \u0001aircraft\u0002 has come to a complete stop.","請保持坐著,直到「繫安全帶」燈號熄滅且飛機完全停妥。"],["leader-112-44","This is a non-smoking flight. Please be aware that smoking is prohibited on the entire \u0001aircraft\u0002.","本班機為禁菸航班。請注意,全機禁止吸菸。"]],"allergic (adj.)":[["guide-113-60","Many people are \u0001allergic\u0002 to pollen, and they experience symptoms like sneezing and itchy eyes during spring.","許多人對花粉過敏,他們在春天會出現打噴嚏、眼睛癢等症狀。"],["leader-112-66","B: Doctor, it seems I am \u0001allergic\u0002 to seafood.",""]],"architect (n.)":[["guide-112-51","Designed by British \u0001architects\u0002, the hotel can accommodate more than 700 people.","這家由英國建築師設計的飯店可容納超過 700 人。"],["leader-111-17","In 1666, the Great Fire burnt for three days and destroyed most buildings in London. The famous \u0001architect\u0002, Christopher Wren, designed many buildings after the Great Fire.","1666 年倫敦大火燒了三天,摧毀多數建築。著名建築師 Christopher Wren 在大火後設計了許多建築。"]],"arrange (v.)":[["guide-112-61","A concierge is someone who is employed in a hotel to help guests \u0001arrange\u0002 things, such as local tours, theatre tickets and restaurant reservations.","禮賓員是飯店雇用來協助客人安排事務(如當地旅遊、劇院票券和餐廳訂位)的人。"],["guide-111-66","A: Can I pick up the car at the airport? B: No, but we can \u0001arrange\u0002 for transportation to our lot.","A:我可以在機場取車嗎? B:不行,但我們可以安排交通接送到我們的租車場。"]],"booking (n.)":[["leader-107-63","Many airlines operate overbooking policies because a small number of passengers, having made their \u0001bookings\u0002, do not turn up for their flights.","許多航空公司採超額訂位政策,因為少數已訂位的乘客最後沒現身搭機。"],["leader-106-15","If you want to change your \u0001booking\u0002, we will try to help you, but we cannot guarantee that we will be able to do this.","如果你想改訂位,我們會盡力協助,但我們不能保證一定辦得到。"]],"boutique (n.)":[["leader-115-56","In the areas around this lake, you can find many \u0001boutiques\u0002 selling refined clothes and local handicrafts.","在這座湖周邊,你可以找到許多販售精緻服飾和當地手工藝品的精品店。"],["guide-115-15","In Taiwan, in addition to old-fashioned shopping streets, there are also lavish department stores with designer \u0001boutiques\u0002.","在台灣,除了老式商店街,也有奢華百貨公司,裡面有設計師精品店。"]],"carousel (n.)":[["leader-113-24","I couldn't find it on the \u0001carousel\u0002.",""],["leader-112-8","Normally, checked baggage will be delivered to the \u0001carousel\u0002 after the flight arrives, depending on the priority and the position of baggage.","通常班機抵達後,託運行李會送到行李轉盤,順序視優先級和行李位置而定。"]],"charge (v.)":[["leader-112-47","Changing money at the airport is convenient to get local currency, but you may be \u0001charged\u0002 some service fees.","在機場換錢方便取得當地貨幣,但可能被收手續費。"],["leader-111-20","International calls to mobile phones registered in another country are \u0001charged\u0002 higher rates. The first zero of an international number must be deleted since it is a \"trunk prefix\" only for domestic calls within many countries.","打到在他國註冊的手機的國際電話會被收取較高費率。國際號碼開頭的 0 須刪去,因它是在許多國家只供國內電話使用的「長途字冠」。"]],"chewy (adj.)":[["guide-115-21","Many people in Taiwan like drinking Pearl Milk Tea which usually consists of sweetened tea with milk and \u0001chewy\u0002 tapioca balls.","許多台灣人喜歡喝珍珠奶茶,通常是加了牛奶和有嚼勁粉圓(珍珠)的甜茶。"],["leader-112-30","Bubble tea most commonly consists of tea accompanied by \u0001chewy\u0002 tapioca balls (\"boba\" or \"pearls\").","珍珠奶茶最常見是茶加上有嚼勁的木薯(粉圓)球(即「波霸」或「珍珠」)。"]],"claim (v.)":[["leader-113-62","To \u0001claim\u0002 the tax refund, foreign travelers must apply at the port of their departure from Taiwan within a limited time of their purchase.","要申請退稅,外國旅客須在購買後限定時間內,於離台口岸辦理。"],["leader-112-6","A: Excuse me, I can't find my baggage. B: Do you have your \u0001claim\u0002 tag?","A:不好意思,我找不到行李。 B:你有行李領取牌嗎?"]],"collection (n.)":[["guide-115-62","The National Palace Museum houses the world's largest \u0001collection\u0002 of priceless Chinese art treasures.","故宮博物院收藏著全世界最大的無價中華藝術珍寶典藏。"],["leader-110-77","The decision to turn the Louvre into a massive repository of the world's greatest fine art \u0001collection\u0002 was proposed in 1981 by the French President François Mitterrand.","",4]],"conservation (n.)":[["guide-113-15","The \u0001conservation\u0002 of jungles and rainforests is critical to the survival of many species.","叢林與雨林的保育對許多物種的生存至關重要。"],["guide-113-46","More and more governments are making commitments to sustainable tourism by providing eco-friendly accommodations, \u0001conservation\u0002 efforts, and community engagement initiatives.","越來越多政府承諾推動永續觀光,提供環保住宿、保育行動與社區參與計畫。"]],"conserve (v.)":[["leader-113-33","The Geopark employs various methods to \u0001conserve\u0002 water, including rainwater harvesting and a closed-loop filtration system, while also replacing groundwater with recharge wells.","地質公園採用多種節水方法,包括雨水收集與閉迴路過濾系統,同時也用回補井取代地下水。"],["guide-112-29","Much of Taiwan's natural beauty and wealth are \u0001conserved\u0002 on the east coast of the island.","台灣大部分的自然美景與資源都保存在島嶼東海岸。"]],"consume (v.)":[["guide-110-8","A report indicates that Taiwanese people \u0001consume\u0002 almost 7.9 kilograms of apples per person every year, comparable to the quantity of bananas a Taiwanese has a year.","一份報告指出,台灣人每人每年食用將近 7.9 公斤蘋果,和台灣人一年吃的香蕉量相當。"],["leader-108-72","As a result, the imbalance between what nature replenishes and humans \u0001consume\u0002 will probably continue to grow.","",4]],"cost (n.)":[["leader-114-29","Medical tourism refers to traveling for medical treatment in other countries, often for better services or lower \u0001costs\u0002.","醫療旅遊指的是到其他國家接受醫療治療,通常是為了更好的服務或更低的費用。"],["leader-107-35","Weddings can be expensive. In this week's News Report you can hear about a way to cut the \u0001cost\u0002 of your wedding by 50%.","婚禮可能很花錢。本週新聞報導會告訴你把婚禮費用削減 50% 的方法。"]],"crowded (adj.)":[["guide-113-59","During the tour, the guide highlighted the assembly point in case the group got separated in the \u0001crowded\u0002 area.","導覽途中,導遊特別說明了集合點,以防團體在擁擠處走散。"],["guide-110-3","Telluride, a Victorian-era mining town in Colorado, is a winter paradise offering plenty to do and isn't as \u0001crowded\u0002 as some of Colorado's other destinations.","泰勒瑞德是科羅拉多州一座維多利亞時代的礦業小鎮,是個冬季天堂,有很多活動,也不像科羅拉多其他景點那麼擁擠。"]],"cruise (v.)":[["leader-113-58","\u0001Cruising\u0002 through the Caribbean, passengers enjoyed the warm sea breeze and crystal-clear waters.","搭郵輪航行加勒比海時,乘客享受溫暖海風和清澈海水。"],["leader-110-43","We are currently \u0001cruising\u0002 at an altitude of 3,300 feet at an airspeed of 400 miles per hour.",""]],"deposit (n.)":[["guide-112-41","Sir, we need your \u0001deposit\u0002 for a confirmed and guaranteed reservation.","先生,我們需要您的訂金來完成確認並保證的訂位。"],["leader-111-51","You pay a \u0001deposit\u0002 in advance to secure the reservation.",""]],"device (n.)":[["leader-109-79","Plastics revolutionized medicine with life-saving \u0001devices\u0002, made space travel possible, lightened cars and jets—saving fuel and pollution—and saved lives with helmets, incubators, and equipment for clean drinking water.","",4],["leader-108-10","Captain: Laptop computers and other electronic \u0001devices\u0002 cannot be used until 15 minutes after take-off, or after the seat belt sign has been turned on prior to landing.","機長:筆電和其他電子裝置,須在起飛 15 分鐘後、或降落前安全帶燈亮起後才不能使用。"]],"disrupt (v.)":[["guide-115-76","New findings from Lux Research suggest that while autonomous robotaxis will further \u0001disrupt\u0002 the conventional taxi and ride sharing spaces, car ownership will not be affected.","",1],["leader-114-19","Common sense tells us that behavior that \u0001disrupts\u0002 a classroom and disrupts the learning of others is not acceptable.","常識告訴我們,擾亂課堂、妨礙他人學習的行為是不可接受的。"]],"eligible (adj.)":[["guide-114-14","Foreign travelers who make purchases of at least NT$2,000 on the same day from the same designated stores with the “Taiwan Tax Refund”-label are \u0001eligible\u0002 to request the refund.","外國旅客在同一天於同一貼有「Taiwan Tax Refund」標誌的指定商店消費滿新台幣 2,000 元,即有資格申請退稅。"],["guide-113-36","You just need to find out if your country is \u0001eligible\u0002 for visa-free entry.",""]],"emission (n.)":[["guide-112-71","Unfortunately, airplanes are predicted to triple their CO2 \u0001emissions\u0002 by 2050 if left unchecked now.","",1],["leader-111-63","Many factors contribute to increased level of toxic gases and one factor which is often ignored by people is the \u0001emissions\u0002 of the public transportation.","許多因素導致有毒氣體增加,其中常被人們忽略的一項是大眾運輸的排放。"]],"erupt (v.)":[["guide-115-40","The volcano on the island has been unusually active over the past few days; many residents are afraid that it is going to \u0001erupt\u0002 in no time.","島上的火山過去幾天異常活躍;許多居民擔心它很快就要噴發。"],["leader-113-11","The geyser \u0001erupts\u0002 more frequently than any of the other big ones and is still as spectacular as it was a century ago.","這座間歇泉噴發比其他大型間歇泉更頻繁,至今仍和一世紀前一樣壯觀。"]],"essential (adj.)":[["leader-113-65","Before you undertake a journey through the Amazon rainforest, it's \u0001essential\u0002 to be well-prepared and informed.","在你展開穿越亞馬遜雨林的旅程前,充分準備和了解資訊至關重要。"],["guide-111-20","Shopping has converted into an \u0001essential\u0002 factor for many tourists when choosing a travel destination.","對許多遊客而言,購物已轉變成選擇旅遊目的地時的重要因素。"]],"exhibit (n.)":[["leader-115-60","In many museums, touching the \u0001exhibited\u0002 items is a behavior that is absolutely prohibited.","在許多博物館,觸摸展示品是絕對被禁止的行為。"],["guide-113-30","The controversial art \u0001exhibit\u0002 was designed to provoke thought and discussion among its viewers.","這場具爭議的藝術展旨在激發觀眾的思考與討論。"]],"expire (v.)":[["guide-114-70","In international practice, most countries and territories may refuse entry to a foreign visitor if their passport will \u0001expire\u0002 less than six months after the date of arrival.","依國際慣例,若外國旅客的護照在抵達日後不到六個月就到期,多數國家與地區可能拒絕其入境。"],["guide-112-44","Only when David was stopped by a policeman for drunk driving did he realize that his passport had \u0001expired\u0002 and he was forced to return home.","直到 David 因酒駕被警察攔下,他才意識到護照已過期,並被迫返國。"]],"habitat (n.)":[["guide-115-42","The rich topographic features and diverse vegetation of Taroko National Park bring about a variety of \u0001habitats\u0002 in which many life forms thrive.","太魯閣國家公園豐富的地形與多樣的植被,孕育出各種棲地,眾多生命形式在其中繁衍。"],["guide-114-68","The lowlands of Taiwan, especially the coasts, are important \u0001habitats\u0002 for seabirds and for wildlife associated with the few remaining undisturbed patches of tropical strand or mangrove trees.","台灣的低地,尤其是海岸,是海鳥及與少數僅存未受干擾的熱帶海濱林或紅樹林相關野生動物的重要棲地。"]],"inexpensive (adj.)":[["leader-113-60","In Europe, where travel distances are often short, it is usually more convenient and \u0001inexpensive\u0002 to travel by train than by airplane.","在歐洲,由於旅行距離常常很短,搭火車通常比搭飛機更方便且便宜。"],["guide-113-61","In Taiwan, you don't need to worry about traveling far to find eateries that offer \u0001inexpensive\u0002 food.","在台灣,你不用擔心要跑很遠才能找到提供便宜食物的餐館。"]],"insurance (n.)":[["guide-114-52","If you do not have appropriate \u0001insurance\u0002 before you travel, you could be liable for emergency expenses.","如果你在旅行前沒有適當的保險,可能需要自行負擔緊急費用。"],["leader-111-57","If you are sick when travelling, you could call the hospital and schedule an appointment. When you visit the hospital, you need to bring your health \u0001insurance\u0002 policy documents.","旅途中生病,可打電話給醫院預約。看診時要帶健康保險保單文件。"]],"issue (v.)":[["guide-113-16","Due to increased demand, the national park started \u0001issuing\u0002 more permits for overnight camping to accommodate more hikers.","由於需求增加,國家公園開始發放更多過夜露營許可證,以容納更多登山客。"],["leader-111-13","They can't be easily cashed, even at the banks that \u0001issued\u0002 them.",""]],"lantern (n.)":[["leader-115-11","The view gets even more romantic at night as cherry trees along the river are lighted up by charming paper \u0001lanterns\u0002.","夜裡景色更浪漫,沿河的櫻花樹被迷人的紙燈籠點亮。"],["guide-114-28","The Pingxi \u0001Lantern\u0002 Festival in New Taipei City is known as one of the best festivals in Taiwan. Thousands of lanterns are sent into the air as a form of prayer for good luck and blessings.","新北市的平溪天燈節是台灣最棒的節慶之一。成千上萬的天燈升空,作為祈求好運與祝福的一種方式。"]],"meal (n.)":[["guide-112-63","If you are not hungry, we can order one \u0001meal\u0002 and share it. The portions are very big.","如果你不餓,我們可以點一份餐一起分。這裡的份量很大。"],["leader-108-36","Do not undertake hard exercise for a few hours after a \u0001meal\u0002 to allow food to digest.","飯後幾小時內不要做劇烈運動,好讓食物消化。"]],"missing (adj.)":[["leader-113-24","I'm reporting a \u0001missing\u0002 suitcase.",""],["leader-112-31","You can go to the Lost and Found Service Center for your \u0001missing\u0002 items.","你可以到失物招領中心找你遺失的物品。"]],"operate (v.)":[["guide-115-60","Before departure, please check the airline's official website to confirm that your flight is \u0001operating\u0002 normally.","出發前,請查看航空公司官方網站,確認你的航班正常運作。"],["leader-111-45","Passenger: Could you show me how to \u0001operate\u0002 the in-flight entertainment?",""]],"operator (n.)":[["guide-114-44","The travel business has shown clearly that the largest setbacks came among the relatively cheap package tour \u0001operators\u0002, and especially with tours that have a low foreign currency content.","旅遊業已清楚顯示,最大的挫敗(衰退)發生在相對便宜的套裝行程業者身上,尤其是外幣占比低的行程。"],["leader-111-38","Guest: Please transfer my call to an international \u0001operator\u0002.",""]],"option (n.)":[["leader-114-80","Unlike traditional vacation cruises, the Odyssey offers a new growing trend: cruises are a new living \u0001option\u0002 for the rich.","",4],["guide-112-19","While beef may seem like a great choice for holidays and other special occasions, some research suggests it may not be the healthiest \u0001option\u0002.","雖然牛肉在節慶和其他特殊場合看似是絕佳選擇,但有些研究指出它可能不是最健康的選項。"]],"pandemic (n.)":[["guide-110-6","Despite global restrictions on travel due to the coronavirus \u0001pandemic\u0002, travel between the United States and Mexico has continued relatively unchecked through 2020.","儘管因新冠疫情全球對旅行實施限制,美墨之間的旅行在整個 2020 年仍相對不受阻礙地持續著。"],["guide-110-7","Air travel in the US took its biggest dive since World War II at the beginning of the \u0001pandemic\u0002 in 2020.",""]],"pharmacy (n.)":[["leader-114-35","Kate: Could you please tell me where the \u0001pharmacy\u0002 is?",""],["guide-113-57","The \u0001pharmacy\u0002 is where you can fill your prescriptions and purchase over-the-counter medications and health-related products.","藥局是你可以領處方藥、購買成藥與健康相關產品的地方。"]],"preference (n.)":[["leader-114-47","Wilson: Before we leave for the trip, can you fill out this questionnaire about your \u0001preferences\u0002?",""],["leader-114-71","Most travelers have a \u0001preference\u0002 for window or aisle seats when it comes to air travel, but have you ever given thought to which side of the plane you should sit on?","",4]],"preserve (v.)":[["guide-114-5","The historical value of the museum lies in its exterior design which \u0001preserves\u0002 the architectural trends of the early 20th century.","博物館的歷史價值在於其外觀設計保留了 20 世紀初的建築風潮。"],["leader-113-68","Tourists should always abide by the rules and regulations of the national parks they visit to \u0001preserve\u0002 the natural environment.","遊客應始終遵守所造訪國家公園的規章,以保護自然環境。"]],"promote (v.)":[["leader-111-54","Visitor Information Center could \u0001promote\u0002 regional tourism since it provides free information and encourages tourists to participate in local events and visit local attractions.","遊客服務中心能促進區域觀光,因它提供免費資訊,鼓勵遊客參與在地活動、造訪當地景點。"],["guide-111-15","Tourism is vital to the economy of a country; as a result, the National Tourism Authorities always try to \u0001promote\u0002 its national brand image.","觀光對一國經濟至關重要;因此,國家觀光機關總是努力推廣其國家品牌形象。"]],"purchase (n.)":[["guide-111-55","You can make big \u0001purchases\u0002 with your credit card. That way, you don't have to carry large amounts of cash.","你可以用信用卡進行大額消費(購物)。這樣就不必攜帶大量現金。"],["leader-110-21","That sign on the wall says 20 percent off on all \u0001purchases\u0002.",""]],"receptionist (n.)":[["leader-113-12","The \u0001receptionist\u0002 of a hotel is responsible for politely completing the check-in procedure and introducing the facilities and services the hotel provides.","飯店櫃台負責禮貌地完成入住手續,並介紹飯店提供的設施和服務。"],["leader-110-49","Traveler: May I have a local map? \u0001Receptionist\u0002: Sure, here you go.","旅客:能給我一張當地地圖嗎? 櫃台:當然,拿去吧。"]],"regulation (n.)":[["guide-114-9","Tour guides should be well-versed in the local history, landmarks, culture, and \u0001regulations\u0002.","導遊應對當地歷史、地標、文化與法規十分熟稔。"],["leader-113-68","Tourists should always abide by the rules and \u0001regulations\u0002 of the national parks they visit to preserve the natural environment.","遊客應始終遵守所造訪國家公園的規章,以保護自然環境。"]],"resident (n.)":[["leader-114-78","Also, wealthy \u0001residents\u0002 do not want to share their space with tourists.","",4],["leader-112-78","In Taiwan, Xiaoliuqiu (also called Little Liuqiu or Liuqiu), an island belonging to Pingtung County in Taiwan has a high number of sea turtles, and the majority of the \u0001residents\u0002 there have been aware of the importance of protecting sea turtles.","",4]],"restore (v.)":[["guide-113-71","Which of the following is closest in meaning to the word “\u0001restored\u0002” in the first paragraph?","下列何者與第一段的 restored 意思最接近?"],["guide-113-71","Due to natural disaster and damages caused by humans, the temple has been \u0001restored\u0002 several times.","",1]],"return (v.)":[["leader-113-41","Customer: I'd like to \u0001return\u0002 this blender.",""],["guide-112-46","If you are not completely satisfied with our product, you can \u0001return\u0002 it for a full refund.","如果你對我們的產品不完全滿意,可以退貨並獲得全額退款。"]],"ride (n.)":[["guide-114-29","Now many tourists come here to experience the \u0001ride\u0002.",""],["guide-113-6","It'll be about a 20-minute \u0001ride\u0002 to the hotel.",""]],"skyscraper (n.)":[["guide-115-65","Designed to look like a pole of bamboo, this \u0001skyscraper\u0002 is the tallest and most iconic landmark of the city.","這棟以竹節造型設計的摩天大樓(台北 101),是該市最高、最具代表性的地標。"],["leader-108-28","The Burj Khalifa is a \u0001skyscraper\u0002 in Dubai and has been the tallest building in the world since 2008.","哈里發塔是杜拜的一座摩天大樓,自 2008 年以來一直是世界最高的建築。"]],"snorkeling (n.)":[["guide-114-25","If you are staying near the coast in Taiwan, some homestays might offer activities like \u0001snorkeling\u0002 in the sea.","如果你在台灣海邊住宿,有些民宿可能提供像浮潛這類的海上活動。"],["leader-112-76","They come for scuba diving, SUP (stand-up paddling), \u0001snorkeling\u0002, and so on.","",1]],"steak (n.)":[["guide-113-4","Waitress: How would you like your \u0001steak\u0002?",""],["guide-113-54","Tour Leader: One of our guests absolutely loved the \u0001steak\u0002 tonight.",""]],"takeoff (n.)":[["leader-114-53","Before \u0001takeoff\u0002 and landing, flight attendants instruct passengers to place their seats in the upright position.","起飛和降落前,空服員指示乘客把座椅調到直立位置。"],["leader-113-61","All mobile phones must be switched to flight mode before \u0001takeoff\u0002 and landing.","所有手機在起飛和降落前必須切換到飛航模式。"]],"temple (n.)":[["leader-115-37","Tourist: Can we take photos inside the \u0001temple\u0002? Tour Guide: Yes, but please turn off the camera flash.","遊客:我們可以在寺廟內拍照嗎? 導遊:可以,但請關閉相機閃光燈。"],["guide-115-31","Longshan \u0001Temple\u0002, located in Wanhua, is one of Taipei's finest examples of Taiwan's architectural and historical heritage.","位於萬華的龍山寺,是台灣建築與歷史遺產的最佳範例之一。"]],"tip (n.)":[["leader-115-46","These essential travel \u0001tips\u0002 will help you avoid common travel mistakes and make the most of your journey.","這些必備的旅遊訣竅能幫你避免常見的旅行錯誤,充分享受旅程。"],["guide-109-21","When you tell the driver to “keep the change,” you are giving the change as a \u0001tip\u0002.","當你跟司機說「不用找了」,你是把找的零錢當小費給他。"]],"trail (n.)":[["guide-115-22","The \u0001trail\u0002 around Sun Moon Lake in Nantou is listed as one of the 10 best cycling routes in the world by CNN.","南投日月潭的環湖步道被 CNN 列為全球十大最佳自行車路線之一。"],["leader-114-11","Many national parks have \u0001trails\u0002 and reachable adventures, allowing everyone to enjoy the beauty of America's protected spaces.","許多國家公園有步道和可及的探險活動,讓每個人都能享受美國受保護空間之美。"]],"transportation (n.)":[["leader-115-14","To make getting around the city easier, the tour leader suggested that everyone buy a \u0001transportation\u0002 pass, which allows unlimited travel on buses and trains for a set period.","為了方便在市區移動,領隊建議大家買一張交通票券,可在一段期間內無限搭乘公車和火車。"],["leader-111-11","Receptionist: Our one-day package tour includes a guided tour of the city and free \u0001transportation\u0002. Guest: That sounds perfect.","櫃台:我們的一日套裝行程含城市導覽和免費接送(交通)。 客人:聽起來很完美。"]],"validity (n.)":[["leader-115-64","It is common sense that before booking your international flight, you should always check the \u0001validity\u0002 of your passport to ensure it meets the entry requirements for your destination country.","常識是,預訂國際航班前,你應該先檢查護照的有效性(效期),以確保符合目的地國的入境要求。"],["leader-113-76","First, the \u0001validity\u0002 of your passport can be an easy oversight.","",1]],"viable (adj.)":[["guide-115-19","If your goal is to catch an early High-Speed Rail (HSR) train to Taichung, the 6:00 A.M. MRT is the earliest \u0001viable\u0002 option from the airport.","如果你的目標是搭早班高鐵到台中,清晨 6 點的捷運是從機場出發最早、可行的選擇。"],["leader-114-80","What does the word \"\u0001viable\u0002\" (in the last paragraph) mean?","(最後一段中)「viable」一字的意思是?"]],"visa (n.)":[["leader-115-32","Officers at immigration check all passports and \u0001visas\u0002 before travelers can enter the country.","入境查驗處的官員會查驗所有護照和簽證,旅客才能入境。"],["leader-115-62","Aliens who overstay their \u0001visas\u0002 would be deported back to their country of birth.","逾期居留簽證的外國人會被遣返回其出生國。"]],"access (n.)":[["leader-115-67","That museum is very old and not friendly to tourists who need elevator \u0001access\u0002.","那間博物館很老舊,對需要電梯通道(使用)的遊客不太友善。"],["guide-115-39","In Taiwan, special rental places such as \"whole-house lodging\" can be found. You can rent a whole house just for your party and have \u0001access\u0002 to your own private facilities.","在台灣可找到「整棟出租(包棟民宿)」這類特別的租宿。你可以只為自己的團體租下整棟房子,擁有使用自己專屬設施的權利。"]],"accident (n.)":[["leader-112-20","We missed the warning signs and that's why the car \u0001accident\u0002 happened.","我們錯過了警告標誌,所以才發生車禍。"],["leader-111-16","Tourist: Sir, a car \u0001accident\u0002 just happened across the street.",""]],"accompany (v.)":[["leader-110-14","Fresh herbs such as chives and parsley are essential ingredients in the sauces that \u0001accompany\u0002 most French savory dishes.","細香蔥、巴西里等新鮮香草是醬汁的必要食材,這些醬汁搭配多數法式鹹食。"],["guide-109-52","Let me remind you that all children must be \u0001accompanied\u0002 by an adult in the art center.","提醒你,在藝術中心所有孩童都必須有大人陪同。"]],"account (n.)":[["leader-111-64","At public places such as libraries, hotels, and airports, free Wi-Fi is very convenient but not secure. Travelers should avoid logging into bank \u0001accounts\u0002 and entering passwords at these public areas because someone else might see them.","在圖書館、飯店、機場等公共場所,免費 Wi-Fi 很方便但不安全。旅客應避免在這些公共區域登入銀行帳戶或輸入密碼,以免被他人看到。"],["leader-107-60","When you are traveling, try to avoid logging into bank \u0001accounts\u0002 or entering any passwords while using free public WiFi at a place like an airport.","旅行時,在機場等地用免費公共 WiFi,盡量避免登入銀行帳戶或輸入任何密碼。"]],"achieve (v.)":[["leader-115-58","Find out why customers have come on holidays, what they want to do, and then help them to \u0001achieve\u0002 their dream.","找出顧客為何來度假、他們想做什麼,然後幫他們實現夢想。"],["leader-115-80","According to the text, which of the following is necessary to \u0001achieve\u0002 net zero before 2050?","根據本文,下列何者是 2050 年前達成淨零的必要條件?"]],"affordable (adj.)":[["leader-112-40","Taiwan has become more and more popular among foreign tourists because it is quite \u0001affordable\u0002 and friendly.","台灣越來越受外國旅客歡迎,因為它相當物價實惠又友善。"],["guide-112-7","She is now looking for \u0001affordable\u0002 airline tickets in order to return to her homeland soon.","她現在正在找負擔得起的機票,以便盡快返回家鄉。"]],"airsickness (n.)":[["leader-112-10","Flight attendant: You seem to have some \u0001airsickness\u0002. B: Yes, do you have medicine for that?","空服員:您似乎有點暈機。 乘客:是的,你們有暈機藥嗎?"],["leader-112-45","Here is the \u0001airsickness\u0002 bag, right in front of your seat pocket.",""]],"amenity (n.)":[["guide-113-27","The new luxury hotel boasts a capacity of 500 guests, offering them unparalleled comfort and \u0001amenities\u0002.","這家新的豪華飯店以可容納 500 位客人的容量自豪,為他們提供無與倫比的舒適與設施。"],["guide-112-12","Most premium airlines provide passengers with superior levels of comfort, seats, \u0001amenities\u0002, and luggage management.","大多數高級航空公司為乘客提供更優越的舒適度、座椅、設施與行李管理。"]],"apologize (v.)":[["leader-114-27","I \u0001apologize\u0002 on behalf of the company for our waitress's error, and we will cover the cost of dry cleaning.","我代表公司為我們服務生的錯誤道歉,我們會負擔乾洗費用。"],["leader-113-19","This is your captain speaking. We \u0001apologize\u0002 for our late departure, but as is sometimes the case at San Francisco, the fog was too thick for taking off.","我是機長。我們為延遲起飛道歉,但如舊金山常有的情況,霧太濃無法起飛。"]],"appetizer (n.)":[["guide-113-44","The restaurant's \u0001appetizers\u0002, including crispy calamari, stuffed mushrooms, and savory sliders, left us eagerly anticipating the main course.","這家餐廳的開胃菜,包括酥炸花枝、鑲蘑菇和美味小漢堡,讓我們熱切期待主餐。"],["leader-107-18","We ordered two \u0001appetizers\u0002, chicken wings and Mozzarella sticks, salad and soup before the main dish.","我們在主菜前點了兩道開胃菜——雞翅和莫札瑞拉起司條、沙拉和湯。"]],"appliance (n.)":[["guide-115-57","Taiwan uses electric current of 110 volts at 60 cycles; \u0001appliances\u0002 from Europe, Australia, or South-East Asia will need a(n) converter or transformer.","台灣使用 110 伏特、60 赫茲的電流;來自歐洲、澳洲或東南亞的電器會需要轉換器或變壓器。"],["guide-114-15","Taiwan uses electric current of 110 volts at 60 cycles, so \u0001appliances\u0002 from Europe, Australia or South-East Asia will need an adapter or transformer.","台灣使用 110 伏特、60 赫茲的電流,所以來自歐洲、澳洲或東南亞的電器會需要轉接器或變壓器。"]],"application (n.)":[["guide-115-47","It takes approximately five working days (excluding weekends and national holidays) to process passport \u0001applications\u0002.","護照申請的辦理大約需要五個工作天(不含週末與國定假日)。"],["leader-112-12","To maintain your rights, please arrive at the airport three hours prior to your departure time for tax refund \u0001application\u0002.","為保障權益,請於出發前三小時抵達機場辦理退稅申請。"]],"architecture (n.)":[["leader-115-68","The \u0001architecture\u0002 of this building is typical of the Renaissance age, and many tourists enjoy visiting this place.","這棟建築的建築(風格)是文藝復興時期的典型,許多遊客喜歡來參觀。"],["guide-114-32","The \u0001architecture\u0002 of the Old Taichung Train Station is a mix of traditional Japanese and late Renaissance themes. It is now listed as a national monument.","台中舊火車站的建築融合了傳統日式與晚期文藝復興的風格。它現在被列為國定古蹟。"]],"arrival (n.)":[["leader-115-34","The crowd waited anxiously at the terminal for the \u0001arrival\u0002 of the VIP guests.","群眾在航廈焦急地等待貴賓的到來。"],["guide-109-68","If you find your baggage damaged after the \u0001arrival\u0002 of your flight, report to the Airport Service Office immediately.","若你在班機抵達後發現行李受損,請立刻向機場服務處通報。"]],"artifact (n.)":[["leader-114-55","The team made an incredible discovery at the archaeological site, uncovering \u0001artifacts\u0002 that were thousands of years old.","團隊在考古遺址有驚人發現,挖掘出數千年前的文物。"],["guide-114-33","The National Palace Museum is home to hundreds of thousands of ancient Chinese \u0001artifacts\u0002 and artwork, which are of great historical value.","故宮博物院收藏著數十萬件古代中華文物與藝術品,深具歷史價值。"]],"atmosphere (n.)":[["leader-115-10","This ancient city is a must-visit destination for every tourist to experience the traditional culture and old town \u0001atmosphere\u0002.","這座古城是每位遊客必訪的目的地,可體驗傳統文化與老城氛圍。"],["leader-109-24","Natalie: I like the \u0001atmosphere\u0002 in your restaurant.",""]],"authorities (n.)":[["leader-113-14","The \u0001authorities\u0002 have touted their efforts in protecting the environment during the $2 billion project.","當局在這 20 億美元的計畫中大力標榜他們保護環境的努力。"],["guide-113-31","In the unfortunate event of a group member's accidental demise during a foreign trip, it is necessary to obtain an official death certificate from local \u0001authorities\u0002.",""]],"aviation (n.)":[["guide-112-73","The \u0001aviation\u0002 sector has released huge amounts of carbon dioxide (CO2) into the atmosphere every year.","",4],["leader-111-69","Pilots and air traffic controllers are all proficient in \u0001aviation\u0002 English as well as everyday English.","機師和航管人員都精通航空英語和日常英語。"]],"baggage (n.)":[["guide-113-21","First, your \u0001baggage\u0002 pick-up time is 9:00 a.m. tomorrow morning, and please have all your baggage ready and put them outside your room by 9:00 a.m.",""],["leader-112-6","A: Excuse me, I can't find my \u0001baggage\u0002. B: Do you have your claim tag?","A:不好意思,我找不到行李。 B:你有行李領取牌嗎?"]],"ban (v.)":[["guide-110-4","Taiwan has become the first country in Asia to totally \u0001ban\u0002 the eating of dog and cat meat, and violating the rule is punishable by up to $8,000 in fines.","台灣成為亞洲第一個完全禁止食用貓狗肉的國家,違規者最高可罰 8,000 元。"],["guide-110-52","The temple is unique in that the burning of incense is \u0001banned\u0002 in the interest of the environment.","這座廟宇獨特之處在於,為了環境,禁止燒香。"]],"bargain (n.)":[["leader-111-24","It is already a real \u0001bargain\u0002.",""],["guide-109-56","I heard books are on sale in the store this month. Maybe we can get a good \u0001bargain\u0002 there.","我聽說這個月書店特價,也許我們能在那撿到划算貨。"]],"beverage (n.)":[["guide-114-35","Drink stores can be found practically anywhere in built-up areas in Taiwan. Most of the \u0001beverages\u0002 at these places involve tea.","在台灣的鬧區幾乎到處都能找到飲料店。這些店裡大部分的飲料都含茶。"],["leader-109-46","Non-alcoholic \u0001beverages\u0002 are complimentary on all the flights. You don't have to pay for them.","所有航班上的無酒精飲料都是免費招待的,你不用付錢。"]],"bicycle (n.)":[["leader-109-66","This is a city for \u0001bicycles\u0002 and more tourists are adopting this way of exploring the city.","這是座適合單車的城市,越來越多遊客採用這種探索城市的方式。"],["guide-108-33","On the MRT of Taiwan, visitors carrying \u0001bicycles\u0002 can get on and off the train only at designated stations.","在台灣捷運,攜帶單車的旅客只能在指定車站上下車。"]],"biodiversity (n.)":[["guide-115-71","Drawing on Alishan's ecological treasures, the train blends striking design with the experience of exploring Alishan's rich \u0001biodiversity\u0002, making the Vivid Express a truly unique journey.","",1],["leader-113-45","Ecological tourism encourages sustainable travel, fostering appreciation for natural wonders while promoting conservation efforts crucial for preserving our planet's \u0001biodiversity\u0002.","生態旅遊鼓勵永續旅行,培養對自然奇景的欣賞,同時推動對保護地球生物多樣性至關重要的保育工作。"]],"block (n.)":[["leader-114-35","When you leave the hotel, turn left and go straight for two \u0001blocks\u0002 until you get to the intersection.",""],["leader-113-38","You need to head down this street, and it's just a few \u0001blocks\u0002 that way.",""]],"board (v.)":[["guide-115-58","You need a passport to \u0001board\u0002 an international flight and to enter a country.","你需要護照才能登上國際航班並進入一個國家。"],["leader-110-46","Flight attendants can help travelers with young kids to \u0001board\u0002 earlier for their convenience.","空服員可協助帶幼童的旅客提早登機,以方便他們。"]],"border (n.)":[["leader-114-70","The inspector expressed his concerns about the lack of an adequate effort to enforce customs laws along the \u0001border\u0002.","稽查員表達他對邊境缺乏足夠努力執行海關法規的擔憂。"],["leader-110-61","Due to the influences of the COVID-19, our \u0001border\u0002 has been closed since last March.","由於 COVID-19 的影響,我們的國界自去年三月起關閉。"]],"browse (v.)":[["leader-109-52","Clerk: Can I help you find anything? Customer: I'm just \u0001browsing\u0002.","店員:需要我幫你找什麼嗎? 顧客:我只是隨便看看。"],["guide-108-52","For some passengers, \u0001browsing\u0002 the duty-free catalogue during the flight is a highlight of the journey.","對某些旅客來說,飛行中瀏覽免稅商品目錄是旅程的一大亮點。"]],"budget (adj.)":[["guide-115-43","By using a variety of cost-cutting strategies, from charging for extras like checked baggage and meals to operating more efficient aircraft, \u0001budget\u0002 airlines have revolutionized air travel, making it accessible to millions.","透過各種削減成本的策略——從托運行李、餐點等額外收費,到操作更省油的飛機——平價航空公司(廉航)徹底革新了航空旅行,讓數百萬人都能負擔。"],["guide-113-62","Hotels operated by chains normally provide accommodations ranging from \u0001budget\u0002 to luxurious ones. However, there are still many privately owned inns and hotels that provide much less expensive rooms and meals than chain hotels.","連鎖經營的飯店通常提供從平價到豪華不等的住宿。然而,仍有許多私人經營的旅館提供比連鎖飯店便宜許多的房間與餐點。"]],"cabin (n.)":[["leader-114-76","Passengers can purchase or rent \u0001cabins\u0002 for up to 15 years.","",1],["leader-112-2","When the pressure drops in the \u0001cabin\u0002, oxygen masks will fall.","當機艙壓力下降時,氧氣面罩會落下。"]],"cash (n.)":[["leader-111-30","Customs officer: Do you have anything to declare? Traveler: Yes, I have NT$100,000 dollars in \u0001cash\u0002 with me.","海關人員:你有任何東西要申報嗎? 旅客:有,我帶了 10 萬元台幣現金。"],["guide-111-55","You can make big purchases with your credit card. That way, you don't have to carry large amounts of \u0001cash\u0002.","你可以用信用卡進行大額消費(購物)。這樣就不必攜帶大量現金。"]],"certificate (n.)":[["leader-111-40","If your passport is lost or stolen abroad, and you need to return to Taiwan right away, you may apply for a(n) \"Entry \u0001Certificate\u0002 for the Republic of China Nationals.\"","若你在國外遺失或被竊護照,又需立刻返台,可申請「中華民國國民入國證明書」。"],["leader-108-65","A marriage \u0001certificate\u0002 is an official statement that two people are married. In most countries, it is issued by a government official only after the civil registration of the marriage.","結婚證書是兩人已婚的官方證明;在多數國家,須待婚姻完成民事登記後,才由政府官員核發。"]],"check-in (n.)":[["guide-114-49","Make sure that your luggage has successfully passed through X-ray inspection before you leave the \u0001check-in\u0002 area.","離開報到區前,請確認你的行李已順利通過 X 光檢查。"],["leader-113-12","The receptionist of a hotel is responsible for politely completing the \u0001check-in\u0002 procedure and introducing the facilities and services the hotel provides.","飯店櫃台負責禮貌地完成入住手續,並介紹飯店提供的設施和服務。"]],"cliff (n.)":[["leader-115-33","Please keep a safe distance between yourself and the \u0001cliff\u0002 edge while taking photos.","拍照時請與懸崖邊緣保持安全距離。"],["guide-115-64","People come to Taroko National Park for its natural wonders. It features majestic \u0001cliffs\u0002, waterfalls, and blue streams.","人們來太魯閣國家公園是為了它的自然奇景。它以雄偉的峭壁、瀑布與湛藍溪流著稱。"]],"coastal (adj.)":[["guide-115-26","Taking up the entire southern tip of Taiwan, Kenting is a \u0001coastal\u0002 playground that lends itself to everything from diving and windsurfing to a growing surfing scene.","佔據台灣最南端的墾丁是個海濱樂園,從潛水、風浪板到日益興盛的衝浪都很適合。"],["guide-113-9","The park's landscape features unique \u0001coastal\u0002 rock formations shaped by natural forces over several million years.","這座公園的地景以…為特色,擁有由自然力量歷經數百萬年塑造的獨特海岸岩層。"]],"commission (n.)":[["guide-112-24","Most tour guides earn \u0001commission\u0002 on sales in addition to their base salary.","大多數導遊除了底薪外,還從銷售中賺取佣金。"],["guide-108-55","If you want to cash your traveler's checks, you must pay a handling charge. We charge a 2% \u0001commission\u0002 on each check.","若你想兌現旅行支票,必須付手續費。我們每張收 2% 佣金。"]],"complaint (n.)":[["leader-109-28","The clerk couldn't deal with the guest's \u0001complaint\u0002, so he asked the manager for help to sort out the problem.","店員無法處理客人的抱怨,所以找經理幫忙解決問題。"],["guide-107-60","One tip for dealing with difficult customers is to put your emotions aside when listening to their \u0001complaints\u0002 or concerns and sincerely thank them for sharing.","應對難纏客人的一個訣竅是:傾聽他們的抱怨或疑慮時放下情緒,並真誠感謝他們分享。"]],"concern (n.)":[["leader-114-15","Scientists found harmful particles in dolphins' breath off Florida, raising \u0001concerns\u0002 for their health and the environment.","科學家在佛州外海海豚的呼吸中發現有害微粒,引發對牠們健康和環境的擔憂。"],["leader-112-75","What is one of the causes that raise people's environmental \u0001concerns\u0002?","引起人們環境關切的原因之一是什麼?"]],"concert (n.)":[["leader-113-22","I have got two complimentary tickets for the \u0001concert\u0002 on next Saturday evening from my boss.",""],["leader-108-39","Many people are queuing up outside the hall for tickets to the \u0001concert\u0002 featuring a talented pianist.","許多人在會堂外排隊買這場才華洋溢鋼琴家演奏會的票。"]],"confiscate (v.)":[["leader-114-46","The security officer had to \u0001confiscate\u0002 the prohibited items from the passenger's luggage.","安檢人員必須從乘客行李中沒收違禁品。"],["leader-113-54","Customs Officer: I'm sorry, sir, but we need to \u0001confiscate\u0002 the fruits in your luggage.",""]],"conflict (n.)":[["guide-113-12","When you are faced with a \u0001conflict\u0002, raising your voice is never a successful way to settle the disagreement.","當你面臨衝突時,提高音量絕不是解決歧見的成功方法。"],["guide-108-62","Since the cessation of the \u0001conflict\u0002 over two decades ago, many people have visited Kinmen, which boasts famous specialties and souvenirs.","自從二十多年前衝突停止以來,許多人造訪金門,那裡以名產與伴手禮聞名。"]],"congestion (n.)":[["guide-114-30","Taiwan's metro system has been praised by locals for its effectiveness in relieving growing traffic \u0001congestion\u0002 in Taipei and its surrounding satellite towns.","台灣的捷運系統因有效紓解台北及周邊衛星城鎮日益嚴重的交通壅塞,而受到當地人稱讚。"],["leader-108-35","Since traffic \u0001congestion\u0002 around the airport is expected during the holidays, travelers should leave home early.","由於假期機場周邊預計會塞車,旅客應提早出門。"]],"connect (v.)":[["leader-115-44","Passenger: Is there Wi-Fi available on this flight? Flight Attendant: Yes, you can \u0001connect\u0002 after takeoff using the instructions provided.","乘客:這班機有 Wi-Fi 嗎? 空服員:有,起飛後你可以依照提供的說明連線。"],["guide-113-77","People are more eager than ever to \u0001connect\u0002 with the real roots of their visiting places.","",4]],"convert (v.)":[["guide-114-43","An interpreter is a person who \u0001converts\u0002 a thought or expression of a source language into an expression with a comparable meaning in a target language.","口譯員是把來源語言的想法或表達轉換成目標語言中意義相當之表達的人。"],["guide-112-8","When traveling abroad, you should carefully choose the money changers to \u0001convert\u0002 currencies.","出國旅行時,你應謹慎選擇換匯處來兌換貨幣。"]],"coupon (n.)":[["guide-112-47","In the travel brochures, you'll find information about tours, itineraries, maps, discounts and \u0001coupons\u0002, or package holidays.","在旅遊簡介手冊裡,你會找到關於行程、路線、地圖、折扣與優惠券,或套裝假期的資訊。"],["leader-109-31","Helen treated everyone from the office to that restaurant because she had a \u0001coupon\u0002 for 30% off.","Helen 請全辦公室的人去那間餐廳,因為她有一張 7 折折價券。"]],"crowd (n.)":[["leader-114-22","At the large, unruly gathering, glass bottles and cans were thrown at police officers as they tried to break up the \u0001crowd\u0002.","在那場大型失序的聚集中,玻璃瓶和罐子被扔向警察,警察試圖驅散人群。"],["guide-109-78","“Bunches of selfie sticks” is an indication of tourist \u0001crowd\u0002.","「成堆的自拍棒」代表什麼?"]],"cruise (n.)":[["leader-114-76","During the pandemic, the \u0001cruise\u0002 industry faced many challenges and financial losses.","",1],["leader-113-9","A: Why do you opt for a \u0001cruise\u0002 holiday? B: Well, I choose it because it offers fully inclusive holidays, which cover meals, entertainment, and tours ashore.","A:你為何選郵輪假期? B:因為它提供全包式假期,含餐點、娛樂和岸上觀光。"]],"customary (adj.)":[["guide-112-21","In many countries, it is \u0001customary\u0002 to leave a gratuity while dining out.","在許多國家,外出用餐時留小費是慣例。"],["guide-108-14","It is \u0001customary\u0002 to leave a tip for your maid.","給房務員留小費是慣例。"]],"delay (n.)":[["leader-114-39","The airline made an announcement over the loudspeaker, informing passengers of a \u0001delay\u0002 due to weather conditions.","航空公司透過廣播系統做了宣布/廣播,告知乘客因天候因素延誤。"],["leader-110-35","We are truly sorry for the \u0001delay\u0002.",""]],"delicacy (n.)":[["guide-115-52","Changhua is noted for its many temples as well as its unique local \u0001delicacies\u0002, such as ba-wan, mao-shu noodle, and braised pork with rice.","彰化以眾多廟宇聞名,也以獨特的在地美食著稱,例如肉圓、貓鼠麵與滷肉飯。"],["guide-110-71","From local \u0001delicacies\u0002 to exotic culinary delights, Taiwan offers a whole array of food choices that cater to all tastes.","",1]],"deliver (v.)":[["leader-106-71","In Hindi, the word dabba refers to lunch box and walla means carrier or \u0001deliver\u0002 man.","",4]],"depart (v.)":[["guide-115-56","Normally, the earliest Airport MRT from Taoyuan International Airport to the Taoyuan HSR Station \u0001departs\u0002 at 6:02 A.M.","通常,從桃園國際機場到桃園高鐵站最早的機場捷運在早上 6:02 發車。"],["guide-111-39","Before going abroad, make sure that your passport must be valid for another six months before you \u0001depart\u0002 for international travel.","出國前,務必確認你的護照在出發做國際旅行前還有至少六個月的有效期。"]],"design (v.)":[["guide-112-51","\u0001Designed\u0002 by British architects, the hotel can accommodate more than 700 people.","這家由英國建築師設計的飯店可容納超過 700 人。"],["leader-111-17","In 1666, the Great Fire burnt for three days and destroyed most buildings in London. The famous architect, Christopher Wren, \u0001designed\u0002 many buildings after the Great Fire.","1666 年倫敦大火燒了三天,摧毀多數建築。著名建築師 Christopher Wren 在大火後設計了許多建築。"]],"detour (n.)":[["leader-112-56","I am afraid that part of the highway to the airport is under construction, so you may need to take a \u0001detour\u0002.","恐怕往機場的部分公路正在施工,所以你可能得繞道。"],["guide-106-5","On multi-lane highways, traffic shifts can be utilized in lieu of a \u0001detour\u0002 as turn lanes can often be congested with detours.","在多線道公路上,可用車道調撥取代改道,因為轉彎車道常因改道而壅塞。"]],"dial (v.)":[["guide-112-13","Do I need to \u0001dial\u0002 the international area code while making a call abroad?","打國際電話時,我需要撥國際區碼嗎?"],["leader-111-14","Foreign guest: How could I use this public phone to make a collect call? Tour leader: Please \u0001dial\u0002 108.","外國客人:我怎麼用這支公共電話打對方付費電話? 領隊:請撥 108。"]],"dimension (n.)":[["leader-112-36","Hand luggage carried aboard aircraft by passengers must be within the following \u0001dimensions\u0002: length 56 cm, width 36 cm, height 23 cm.","乘客帶上機的手提行李須在下列尺寸內:長 56 公分、寬 36 公分、高 23 公分。"]],"diverse (adj.)":[["guide-115-42","The rich topographic features and \u0001diverse\u0002 vegetation of Taroko National Park bring about a variety of habitats in which many life forms thrive.","太魯閣國家公園豐富的地形與多樣的植被,孕育出各種棲地,眾多生命形式在其中繁衍。"],["guide-110-74","As you make your way through different destinations, you are bound to encounter a cultural mosaic of \u0001diverse\u0002 highlights, traditions, and events.","",4]],"dormant (adj.)":[["guide-115-8","Right on Taipei's doorstep, the easy-to-reach national park of Yangmingshan is a geological haven to hiking trails, bubbling hot springs, some challenging cycling routes and several \u0001dormant\u0002 volcanoes.","陽明山國家公園近在台北門口、交通便利,是地質天堂,有步道、沸騰溫泉、具挑戰性的自行車路線和數座休眠火山。"],["leader-113-27","A volcano which has been \u0001dormant\u0002 for nearly two centuries erupted in Iceland last week.","一座休眠近兩世紀的火山上週在冰島噴發。"]],"edge (n.)":[["leader-115-33","Please keep a safe distance between yourself and the cliff \u0001edge\u0002 while taking photos.","拍照時請與懸崖邊緣保持安全距離。"],["leader-111-79","What does the author mean \"Virtual reality can give you an \u0001edge\u0002 over rivals who have not yet adopted it\"?","作者說「VR 能讓你贏過尚未採用它的對手」是什麼意思?"]],"employee (n.)":[["leader-111-74","It is then picked up by an Alibaba \u0001employee\u0002 and carried the rest of the way.","",4],["leader-106-24","An \u0001employee\u0002 who can do business in more than one language is a valuable asset to most companies.","能用多種語言做生意的員工,對多數公司是寶貴的資產。"]],"endangered (adj.)":[["guide-112-76","In my experience, seeing iconic and \u0001endangered\u0002 animals like lions, elephants, and gorillas in their natural habitats is expected to be a staple of a safari vacation.","",1],["guide-111-26","The Formosan black bear is a species indigenous to Taiwan and currently listed as “\u0001endangered\u0002” under Taiwan's Wildlife Conservation Act.","台灣黑熊是原生於台灣的物種,目前依《野生動物保育法》被列為「瀕危」。"]],"enhance (v.)":[["leader-114-49","A nicer room would really \u0001enhance\u0002 our stay.",""],["guide-114-11","An important part of guiding is building rapport with tourists to \u0001enhance\u0002 their experience.","帶團的重要一環是與遊客建立融洽關係,以提升他們的體驗。"]],"erosion (n.)":[["guide-114-65","Uplifting, followed by \u0001erosion\u0002 by rivers, caused the formation of most of the geological features of Taroko Gorge.","地殼抬升,加上河流的侵蝕,造就了太魯閣峽谷大部分的地質特徵。"],["leader-108-75","In West Virginia (USA), for example, loggers in certified forests must receive special training to avoid causing soil \u0001erosion\u0002.","",4]],"escalator (n.)":[["guide-111-12","You can get to Baggage Claim by going down the \u0001escalator\u0002 and following the signs.","你可以下手扶梯後照著標示走到行李提領處。"],["guide-110-48","In case of emergency, open the transparent plastic cover and press the red button to stop the \u0001escalator\u0002.","緊急情況時,打開透明塑膠蓋並按紅色按鈕停止手扶梯。"]],"estimate (v.)":[["guide-113-56","Captain: We're thrilled to have you with us today and hope you're as excited as we are for this journey ahead. Our flight time today is \u0001estimated\u0002 to be approximately five hours.","機長:今天很高興有您同行,希望您和我們一樣期待這趟旅程。今天的飛行時間預估約五小時。"],["guide-113-68","Women are more attracted by spa holidays than men. While spa usage among men is increasing, it was \u0001estimated\u0002 that over 65% of spa customers are female.","女性比男性更受水療假期吸引。雖然男性使用水療的比例在增加,但據估計超過 65% 的水療顧客是女性。"]],"excursion (n.)":[["leader-113-44","During our exciting \u0001excursion\u0002, we explored ancient ruins, savored exotic cuisine, and connected with locals, making our travel unforgettable.","在這趟刺激的短程旅遊中,我們探索古蹟、品嚐異國料理、與當地人交流,讓旅程難忘。"],["guide-111-76","Off-train \u0001excursions\u0002 include a stop in Kimberley, a historical diamond-rush town.","",1]],"exotic (adj.)":[["leader-115-5","If you plan to try some \u0001exotic\u0002 dishes when traveling to a different country, please do some research about what those dishes are.","如果你到不同國家想嘗試一些異國風味的菜,請先研究一下那些是什麼菜。"],["leader-113-44","During our exciting excursion, we explored ancient ruins, savored \u0001exotic\u0002 cuisine, and connected with locals, making our travel unforgettable.","在這趟刺激的短程旅遊中,我們探索古蹟、品嚐異國料理、與當地人交流,讓旅程難忘。"]],"experience (n.)":[["leader-110-3","Tom: Do not go into it for money. The most rewarding aspect of my job is that I go to different places and talk about my own travel \u0001experiences\u0002.","Tom:別為錢入這行。我工作最有成就感的部分,是能到不同地方、分享自己的旅遊經驗。"],["leader-106-28","Anybody looking for a truly heavenly \u0001experience\u0002 will think that they have walked into paradise at the Chocolate Show in New York.","任何想尋求極致美妙體驗的人,到紐約巧克力展會覺得自己彷彿走進了天堂。"]],"feature (n.)":[["leader-114-76","According to the passage, what is the main \u0001feature\u0002 of the Odyssey?","根據本文,Odyssey 的主要特色是什麼?"],["leader-112-74","Which \u0001feature\u0002 are green products known for?","綠色產品以什麼特色聞名?"]],"fee (n.)":[["guide-113-47","A: Is there a complimentary meal on the flight? B: No, but there's a selection of refreshments available for a small \u0001fee\u0002.","A:飛機上有免費餐點嗎? B:沒有,但有一些點心可付少許費用購買。"],["guide-111-13","The last thing you want on a vacation is to find out hidden \u0001fees\u0002 that you must pay.","度假時你最不想遇到的,就是發現隱藏的費用得付。"]],"fermented (adj.)":[["leader-108-8","Tom: What's the signature dish of your restaurant? Attendant: Clay pot chicken in \u0001fermented\u0002 red rice wine.","Tom:你們餐廳的招牌菜是什麼? 服務員:紅糟醃雞煲。"],["guide-108-61","The tofu is left in \u0001fermented\u0002 milk and some ingredients for months, making it pungent and tasty.","豆腐浸在發酵的滷汁與一些原料中數月,讓它變得氣味濃烈又美味(臭豆腐)。"]],"firecracker (n.)":[["guide-114-66","Yenshui Fireworks Festival originated in the past when people would ask the gods for help to get rid of the epidemic in Yenshui, and they would set off \u0001firecrackers\u0002 to welcome the arrival of the gods.","鹽水蜂炮節起源於過去,當時鹽水人祈求神明協助驅除瘟疫,並施放鞭炮迎接神明降臨。"],["guide-109-13","People decorate their homes with plastic \u0001firecrackers\u0002 to ward off bad luck.","人們用塑膠鞭炮裝飾家裡,以驅趕厄運。"]],"flood (n.)":[["guide-113-10","The city was struck by an exceptional high tide, which caused severe \u0001flood\u0002 damage to bridges and roadways.","這座城市遭異常大潮侵襲,造成橋樑與道路嚴重的水患損害。"],["guide-106-16","Tourist deaths have been linked to altitude sickness, \u0001floods\u0002, and hiking accidents over the past decades at Machu Picchu.","過去數十年,馬丘比丘的旅客死亡與高山症、洪水及健行意外有關。"]],"gate (n.)":[["leader-115-30","Mary: John, do you know when boarding will start for our flight? John: Yes, it begins at 9:15 A.M. at \u0001Gate\u0002 7.","Mary:John,你知道我們班機什麼時候開始登機嗎? John:知道,上午 9:15 在 7 號登機門開始。"],["leader-110-44","Clerk: This is the final boarding call for John and Mary Smith booked on flight 321C to Salt Lake City. Please proceed to \u0001gate\u0002 3 immediately.","地勤:這是已訂位飛往鹽湖城 321C 班機的 John 和 Mary Smith 最後登機廣播,請立刻前往 3 號登機門。"]],"geopark (n.)":[["guide-115-54","Along Taiwan's northern coast, the wonders made by nature can be seen at Yehliu \u0001Geopark\u0002. Wind and waves have transformed rocks into various shapes, including a queen with a beautiful, thin neck.","在台灣北部海岸,野柳地質公園可見大自然的鬼斧神工。風與海浪把岩石雕塑成各種形狀,包括有著美麗細頸的女王頭。"],["guide-115-61","The \"Yehliu \u0001Geopark\u0002\" is one of the most famous landmarks of Taiwan.","「野柳地質公園」是台灣最著名的地標之一。"]],"gorge (n.)":[["guide-115-69","The island boasts towering mountains interwoven with \u0001gorges\u0002 and valleys carved out by countless rivers and streams.","這座島擁有高聳的山脈,與無數河流溪水切割出的峽谷、山谷交織在一起。"],["guide-114-65","Uplifting, followed by erosion by rivers, caused the formation of most of the geological features of Taroko \u0001Gorge\u0002.","地殼抬升,加上河流的侵蝕,造就了太魯閣峽谷大部分的地質特徵。"]],"gourmet (adj.)":[["leader-111-59","In a Japanese restaurant, your personal chef brings in the ingredients and cooks the food in front of you. He then serves the steaming hot \u0001gourmet\u0002 dish.","在日式餐廳,你的專屬主廚會端上食材並在你面前烹調,接著上熱騰騰的美食。"],["guide-108-5","First class passengers can enjoy \u0001gourmet\u0002 food.","頭等艙旅客可享用美饌。"]],"gym (n.)":[["guide-112-70","Hotel clerk: We have a bar, a \u0001gym\u0002, a swimming pool, tennis courts and a buffet restaurant.",""],["leader-110-41","Lisa: Do you have any exercise facilities? Hotel clerk: You can go to the 15th floor where our \u0001gym\u0002 is and as long as you have running shoes with you, you can use all of our equipment with no extra charge.","Lisa:你們有健身設施嗎? 櫃台:可以到 15 樓的健身房,只要隨身帶著跑鞋,所有器材都能免費使用。"]],"hospitality (n.)":[["guide-114-76","In the fast-paced and highly competitive world of \u0001hospitality\u0002, where customer expectations are sky-high, the industry faces a multitude of challenges.","",1],["guide-113-42","The politician proposed the loosening of restrictions on foreigners serving in the \u0001hospitality\u0002 and logistics sectors.","這位政治人物提議放寬對在餐旅與物流業工作之外國人的限制。"]],"illegal (adj.)":[["leader-113-79","For instance, chewing gum is \u0001illegal\u0002 in Singapore, feeding pigeons is prohibited in Venice, and riding a cow while intoxicated is not allowed in Scotland.","",4],["leader-113-80","Which of the following is mentioned as an \u0001illegal\u0002 activity in a foreign country?","下列何者被提到是某外國的違法行為?"]],"incentive (n.)":[["leader-114-30","To bring more tourists to Taiwan, the government should offer attractive \u0001incentive\u0002 like discounts and special deals.","為了吸引更多遊客來台灣,政府應提供有吸引力的誘因,例如折扣和特別優惠。"],["leader-111-75","According to the passage, what may not be the \u0001incentive\u0002 for people to use the service of Ele.me food delivery?","根據本文,下列何者可能不是人們使用 Ele.me 外送的誘因?"]],"ingredient (n.)":[["guide-114-26","Common \u0001ingredients\u0002 of Taiwanese cuisine are pork, seafood, rice, soy, and chicken.","台灣料理常見的食材有豬肉、海鮮、米、大豆和雞肉。"],["leader-111-59","In a Japanese restaurant, your personal chef brings in the \u0001ingredients\u0002 and cooks the food in front of you. He then serves the steaming hot gourmet dish.","在日式餐廳,你的專屬主廚會端上食材並在你面前烹調,接著上熱騰騰的美食。"]],"inspection (n.)":[["leader-115-3","Before entering the country, each visitor must have a valid passport ready for \u0001inspection\u0002.","入境前,每位旅客都必須備妥有效護照以供查驗。"],["guide-114-49","Make sure that your luggage has successfully passed through X-ray \u0001inspection\u0002 before you leave the check-in area.","離開報到區前,請確認你的行李已順利通過 X 光檢查。"]],"instruction (n.)":[["leader-115-44","Passenger: Is there Wi-Fi available on this flight? Flight Attendant: Yes, you can connect after takeoff using the \u0001instructions\u0002 provided.","乘客:這班機有 Wi-Fi 嗎? 空服員:有,起飛後你可以依照提供的說明連線。"],["guide-114-16","Abide by all safety rules when enjoying theme-park facilities. To stay safe, listen to what staff members say and follow their \u0001instructions\u0002.","玩主題樂園設施時,請遵守所有安全規定。為了安全,聽從工作人員的話並遵循指示。"]],"issue (n.)":[["leader-112-73","Green consumers are those who are aware of and interested in environmental \u0001issues\u0002.","",4],["guide-112-36","A: Have you had any \u0001issues\u0002 renewing your visa? B: Not yet.","A:你續簽簽證有遇到什麼問題嗎? B:還沒有。"]],"item (n.)":[["leader-112-31","You can go to the Lost and Found Service Center for your missing \u0001items\u0002.","你可以到失物招領中心找你遺失的物品。"],["guide-111-67","I couldn't return this \u0001item\u0002 because I had lost the receipt.","我沒辦法退這件商品,因為我把收據弄丟了。"]],"landing (n.)":[["leader-112-15","Ladies and gentlemen, please fasten your seat belts for \u0001landing\u0002.","各位女士先生,降落前請繫好安全帶。"],["leader-111-31","A cellphone parking lot is a parking lot where people wait for their friends to complete their \u0001landing\u0002 procedures.","「手機停車場」是人們等候朋友完成降落(入境)手續的停車場。"]],"layer (n.)":[["leader-114-25","Remember to wear several \u0001layers\u0002 of clothes to stay warm during travel to protect yourself from the cold.","記得旅行時穿好幾層衣服保暖,保護自己不受寒。"],["guide-107-72","What does the title “A New \u0001Layer\u0002” refer to?","展覽名稱「A New Layer(新的一層)」指的是什麼?"]],"lift (v.)":[["leader-115-57","Passenger: Could you help me place my bag overhead? Flight Attendant: Absolutely, let me \u0001lift\u0002 it for you safely.","乘客:可以幫我把包包放到上方置物櫃嗎? 空服員:當然,我幫你安全抬上去。"],["leader-112-25","Effective from October 13, 2022, Taiwan has \u0001lifted\u0002 the quarantine requirement for all arrivals, so arriving travelers will no longer be required to quarantine.","自 2022 年 10 月 13 日起,台灣取消所有入境者的隔離要求,入境旅客不再須隔離。"]],"luxury (n.)":[["guide-110-71","Traveling in Taiwan is a \u0001luxury\u0002 that anyone can enjoy without spending a fortune.","",1],["guide-106-71","The Tour de France has cycling on many people's minds, and for \u0001luxury\u0002 travelers, there has never been a better time to tour the world on two wheels.","",4]],"medicine (n.)":[["leader-112-10","Flight attendant: You seem to have some airsickness. B: Yes, do you have \u0001medicine\u0002 for that?","空服員:您似乎有點暈機。 乘客:是的,你們有暈機藥嗎?"],["leader-109-14","Many \u0001medicines\u0002 must be prescribed by a doctor. You cannot buy them at the pharmacy.","許多藥物必須由醫生開立處方,你無法在藥局直接買。"]],"migration (n.)":[["leader-114-10","Leaders of European Union countries arrived in Brussels for a summit, where \u0001migration\u0002 is an urgent topic.","歐盟各國領袖抵達布魯塞爾參加高峰會,移民是緊急議題。"],["leader-112-76","The team observes the life of sea turtles, keeping records of their \u0001migration\u0002 behaviors.","",1]],"monument (n.)":[["guide-114-32","The architecture of the Old Taichung Train Station is a mix of traditional Japanese and late Renaissance themes. It is now listed as a national \u0001monument\u0002.","台中舊火車站的建築融合了傳統日式與晚期文藝復興的風格。它現在被列為國定古蹟。"],["leader-112-59","We can take the subway to the \u0001monument\u0002.",""]],"nostalgia (n.)":[["guide-109-33","Taiwan Railways offers \u0001nostalgia\u0002 bento, transporting memories, __BLANK2__ for home, and tales of goodness.","台鐵推出懷舊便當,承載回憶、思鄉之情與美好故事。"],["guide-107-79","Which is closest in meaning to the word “\u0001nostalgia\u0002” in the second paragraph?","第二段中的「nostalgia」一詞意思最接近下列何者?"]],"offer (v.)":[["guide-113-61","In Taiwan, you don't need to worry about traveling far to find eateries that \u0001offer\u0002 inexpensive food.","在台灣,你不用擔心要跑很遠才能找到提供便宜食物的餐館。"],["leader-112-19","The hotel \u0001offers\u0002 easy access to the National Palace Museum.","這間飯店可輕鬆前往國立故宮博物院。"]],"overcharge (v.)":[["leader-110-36","I only bought a pair of blue jeans at US$20, but here it says US$40. You seem to have \u0001overcharged\u0002 me.","我只買一條 20 美元的牛仔褲,但這裡寫 40 美元。你好像多收我錢了。"],["leader-109-40","Front desk clerk: What seems to be the problem with your invoice? Hotel Guest: I think I have been \u0001overcharged\u0002.","櫃台:你的帳單有什麼問題嗎? 飯店客人:我覺得我被多收費了。"]],"overweight (adj.)":[["leader-110-58","Clerk: Your luggage seems \u0001overweight\u0002. I will suggest you to find a scale to measure its weight.","櫃台:你的行李好像超重了。我建議你找個磅秤量一下重量。"],["leader-108-4","Please put your suitcase on the scale. Oh, it is \u0001overweight\u0002.","請把行李箱放上磅秤。喔,它超重了。"]],"paradise (n.)":[["guide-110-3","Telluride, a Victorian-era mining town in Colorado, is a winter \u0001paradise\u0002 offering plenty to do and isn't as crowded as some of Colorado's other destinations.","泰勒瑞德是科羅拉多州一座維多利亞時代的礦業小鎮,是個冬季天堂,有很多活動,也不像科羅拉多其他景點那麼擁擠。"],["guide-108-24","An earthly \u0001paradise\u0002 awaits you in the alpine forests of Shei-Pa National Park.","雪霸國家公園的高山森林裡,有人間天堂等著你。"]],"patience (n.)":[["guide-107-77","We are always on the move, and we don't have much \u0001patience\u0002 with slow systems of transportation.","",4],["guide-106-46","Not knowing when the flight was going to take off, some tourists had lost their \u0001patience\u0002 and started yelling at the ground staff.","不知班機何時起飛,有些旅客失去耐心,開始對地勤大吼。"]],"pedestrian (n.)":[["guide-115-35","The buildings are built very close to each other to provide shade for \u0001pedestrians\u0002 walking in the city.","建築物彼此蓋得很近,為在城市中行走的行人提供遮蔭。"],["leader-113-6","Elevated wood-plank bridges are used to separate \u0001pedestrian\u0002 and vehicle traffic, and to provide beautiful views of the treetops.","架高的木棧橋用來區隔行人和車輛,並提供樹梢的美景。"]],"platform (n.)":[["guide-113-65","Clerk: Please mind the gap between the train and the \u0001platform\u0002 when leaving the train.","站務員:下車時請留意火車與月台之間的間隙。"],["leader-109-68","This \u0001platform\u0002 is for southbound trains. Uptown service is on the other side of the tracks.","這個月台是往南的列車。往市區(北)的班車在鐵軌另一側。"]],"pollution (n.)":[["leader-114-21","The global scientific community comes together and calls for immediate action on the urgent global problem—air \u0001pollution\u0002.","全球科學界團結起來,呼籲對空氣污染這個緊急全球問題採取立即行動。"],["guide-113-2","To protect the houses from air \u0001pollution\u0002, a special coating was applied on the exterior surface of the walls for all the houses in the town.","為保護房屋免受空氣污染,鎮上所有房屋的牆面外表都塗上了特殊塗層。"]],"primary (adj.)":[["leader-113-76","What is the \u0001primary\u0002 focus of this passage?","本文的主要焦點為何?"],["guide-110-28","Tour guides' \u0001primary\u0002 responsibility is to make sure the tour is safe for the group of tourists.","導遊的首要責任是確保旅程對整團遊客而言是安全的。"]],"procession (n.)":[["guide-111-27","The annual Dajia Matsu Pilgrimage \u0001procession\u0002 went off without a hitch this year!","今年大甲媽祖遶境進香隊伍順利無阻地完成了!"],["guide-109-35","The \u0001procession\u0002 for the goddess Mazu is a century-old tradition that embodies the collective memories of Taiwanese people.","媽祖遶境是有百年歷史的傳統,體現了台灣人的集體記憶。"]],"prohibit (v.)":[["guide-111-9","Federal law \u0001prohibits\u0002 disabling any smoke detector installed in any airplane lavatory.","聯邦法律禁止停用任何裝在飛機廁所的煙霧偵測器。"],["guide-109-15","Inside the museum, flash photography is strictly \u0001prohibited\u0002.","在博物館內,嚴格禁止使用閃光燈拍照。"]],"provide (v.)":[["leader-111-6","I prefer to pack light. Does your hotel \u0001provide\u0002 free toiletries?","我喜歡輕便打包。你們飯店有提供免費盥洗用品嗎?"],["leader-108-5","The hotel \u0001provides\u0002 two complimentary bottles of water in your fridge.","飯店在你的冰箱裡提供兩瓶免費招待的水。"]],"reception (n.)":[["leader-115-2","Guests checked in at the hotel \u0001reception\u0002 before going to their rooms.","客人先在飯店接待櫃台辦理入住,然後才進房間。"],["guide-108-50","At wedding \u0001receptions\u0002, guests bless the newlyweds by giving them red envelopes filled with money.","在婚宴上,賓客用裝了錢的紅包祝福新人。"]],"recommend (v.)":[["leader-107-43","Tourist: I am looking for a room that would be nice for a romantic weekend. What would you \u0001recommend\u0002?","遊客:我在找適合浪漫週末的房間,你會推薦什麼?"],["guide-107-1","The traveling office \u0001recommended\u0002 10 locations to offer people multiple choices to enjoy the magnificent sunsets in a relaxing way.","這個行動辦公室推薦了 10 個地點,讓人們有多種選擇,悠閒地欣賞壯麗的夕陽。"]],"rehabilitation (n.)":[["leader-113-46","After a severe injury, Hanna underwent intensive \u0001rehabilitation\u0002, working tirelessly to regain her strength, mobility, and independence, ultimately recovering well.","嚴重受傷後,Hanna 接受密集復健,不懈努力以恢復力量、行動力和獨立,最終復原良好。"],["guide-108-73","People can combine hot springs with natural and human resources for relieving stress, \u0001rehabilitation\u0002, and recuperation.","",4]],"renowned (adj.)":[["guide-113-8","The spiritual center of Japan's culture and heritage, Kyoto is \u0001renowned\u0002 for its abundance of green tea.","京都是日本文化與傳統遺產的精神中心,以盛產綠茶聞名。"],["guide-112-17","Yingge District in New Taipei City has been \u0001renowned\u0002 for its pottery for a long time, but recently, tourists have realized that this area offers so much more.","新北市鶯歌區長久以來以陶瓷聞名,但最近遊客發現這個地區能提供的遠不止於此。"]],"represent (v.)":[["leader-115-48","On the city tour, the guide asked everyone to take a photo in front of the famous landmark that \u0001represents\u0002 the history of the area.","市區觀光時,導遊請大家在代表當地歷史的著名地標前拍照。"],["guide-108-2","Embassy is the office that \u0001represents\u0002 your country to a foreign government.","大使館是代表你的國家對外國政府的辦事處。"]],"resemble (v.)":[["leader-114-36","Ground Staff: Can you identify which one \u0001resembles\u0002 your luggage? (Showing a card with various types of luggage.) Amy: Mine looks similar to Type D.","地勤:你能辨認出哪一個像你的行李嗎?(出示各種行李款式的卡片) Amy:我的很像 D 型。"],["guide-112-5","Guabao, a steamed sandwich, \u0001resembles\u0002 a hamburger that has a soft white bun filled with braised pork, pickled vegetables, peanut powder, and cilantro.","刈包是一種蒸的三明治,類似漢堡,有柔軟的白麵皮,夾著滷肉、酸菜、花生粉和香菜。"]],"resilience (n.)":[["guide-114-50","\u0001Resilience\u0002 refers to the ability to successfully adapt to stressors, maintaining psychological well-being in the face of adversity.","韌性(心理復原力)指的是成功適應壓力源、在逆境中維持心理健康的能力。"],["guide-110-78","Indeed, in this ongoing war against the pandemic, we have seen the \u0001resilience\u0002 and power of mankind.","",4]],"responsible (adj.)":[["guide-115-28","With a growing focus on \u0001responsible\u0002 and ethical tourism, sustainable tourism is becoming an increasingly important industry worldwide.","隨著對負責任且合乎道德的觀光日益重視,永續觀光正成為全球日益重要的產業。"],["leader-113-4","\u0001Responsible\u0002 tourists travel with reusable bags and water bottles, with which less trash is created.","負責任的旅客攜帶可重複使用的袋子和水瓶,以減少垃圾。"]],"ritual (n.)":[["leader-115-59","When our group visited a church this morning, we got a glimpse of how the priest performed a local \u0001ritual\u0002.","今早我們團體參觀一間教堂時,得以一瞥神父如何進行當地的儀式。"],["guide-107-13","Wang Ye and Matsu are two of the most common gods in Taiwan, but the \u0001rituals\u0002 of worshipping these gods differ.","王爺與媽祖是台灣民間信仰中最常見的兩位神明,但祭拜這些神明的儀式各有不同。"]],"sanctuary (n.)":[["guide-112-76","Safaris sometimes involve more than just visits to zoos and \u0001sanctuaries\u0002 to see animals; they often provide opportunities for hiking, birdwatching, and cultural immersion.","",1],["guide-111-77","The Koala Gardens, the Australian Butterfly \u0001Sanctuary\u0002, and Bird World Kuranda are among the many attractions in this picturesque village.","",4]],"scale (n.)":[["leader-110-58","Clerk: Your luggage seems overweight. I will suggest you to find a \u0001scale\u0002 to measure its weight.","櫃台:你的行李好像超重了。我建議你找個磅秤量一下重量。"],["leader-108-4","Please put your suitcase on the \u0001scale\u0002. Oh, it is overweight.","請把行李箱放上磅秤。喔,它超重了。"]],"scenery (n.)":[["leader-107-14","We headed to the countryside, rich with gorgeous hills and lakes. The \u0001scenery\u0002 there was breathtaking.","我們前往鄉間,那裡有壯麗的山丘與湖泊。當地景色令人屏息。"],["leader-107-22","There are many different types of \u0001scenery\u0002 in the park. The best way to see them is to go on foot.","公園裡有許多不同的景緻。看它們最好的方式就是步行。"]],"seafood (n.)":[["leader-110-32","I would like a \u0001seafood\u0002 fried rice. Please make it to takeaway.","我要一份海鮮炒飯,請做成外帶。"],["leader-110-42","Mary: I love \u0001seafood\u0002.",""]],"settle (v.)":[["guide-113-12","When you are faced with a conflict, raising your voice is never a successful way to \u0001settle\u0002 the disagreement.","當你面臨衝突時,提高音量絕不是解決歧見的成功方法。"],["guide-111-47","I'd like to leave early tomorrow morning. Can I \u0001settle\u0002 my bill now?","我明天一早想離開。我可以現在結帳嗎?"]],"snack (n.)":[["leader-114-26","The vending machines offer everything you might need, ranging from \u0001snacks\u0002 to pajamas.","自動販賣機提供你可能需要的一切,從零食到睡衣。"],["guide-114-53","Pig's blood cake is a popular Taiwanese street food \u0001snack\u0002 made with pork blood congealed with sticky rice.","豬血糕是受歡迎的台灣街頭小吃,由豬血凝結糯米製成。"]],"statue (n.)":[["leader-113-3","This church dates back to the mid-fourteenth century and houses a large number of remarkable \u0001statues\u0002 and wall paintings.","這座教堂可追溯到 14 世紀中葉,收藏大量傑出的雕像和壁畫。"],["guide-112-20","The Duomo di Milano in Italy has over 3,400 sculptures, making it the place with the most \u0001statues\u0002 in the world.","義大利的米蘭大教堂有超過 3,400 座雕塑,使它成為全世界擁有最多雕像的地方。"]],"stow (v.)":[["guide-114-63","To ensure flight safety, passengers are to safely \u0001stow\u0002 their carry-on baggage under the seat or in the overhead baggage compartment to prevent them from sliding or falling off.","為確保飛航安全,旅客應將隨身行李妥善收放在座位下方或頭頂上方的行李櫃,以防滑動或掉落。"],["guide-112-69","Ladies and gentlemen, please be careful while opening the overhead compartment as any items \u0001stowed\u0002 inside might fall out, and take all your personal belongings with you.","各位女士先生,打開頭頂行李櫃時請小心,因為裡面放的物品可能掉出來;並請帶走所有隨身物品。"]],"subway (n.)":[["leader-112-59","We can take the \u0001subway\u0002 to the monument.",""],["leader-111-49","Many hotels in New York provide free airport shuttle service. You could also take the \u0001subway\u0002 if you are comfortable with public transportation.","紐約許多飯店提供免費機場接駁服務。若你習慣搭大眾運輸,也可搭地鐵。"]],"summit (n.)":[["guide-115-9","Tatajia is the jumping-off point for a variety of forested day hikes, as well as the non-technical, two-day ascent of Jade Peak, with an overnight stay at Paiyun Lodge en route to the \u0001summit\u0002.","塔塔加是各種森林一日健行的起點,也是玉山兩天非技術性攀登的出發點,途中在排雲山莊過夜後前往山頂。"],["guide-115-41","At the \u0001summit\u0002 of Bagua Mountain sits the Eight Trigram Mountains Buddha Landscape, a sight that can be seen from almost anywhere in Changhua City. It is a perfect place to go for a light hike.","八卦山頂坐落著八卦山大佛風景區,幾乎在彰化市任何地方都能看到。這裡是輕鬆健行的絕佳去處。"]],"supply (v.)":[["guide-112-30","A: Does your restaurant \u0001supply\u0002 a continental breakfast? B: Yes, we do, and it's served in a buffet style.","A:你們餐廳有供應歐陸式早餐嗎? B:有的,而且是自助式的。"],["guide-112-72","According to the passage, what is the most common way to \u0001supply\u0002 electricity?","根據本文,供應電力最常見的方式是什麼?"]],"symptom (n.)":[["guide-115-32","Elevations above 700 meters may trigger \u0001symptoms\u0002 of altitude sickness in some individuals, including rapid breathing, increased heart rate, fatigue, asthma, nausea, and vomiting.","海拔 700 公尺以上可能在某些人身上引發高山症的症狀,包括呼吸急促、心跳加快、疲勞、氣喘、噁心與嘔吐。"],["guide-112-59","Doctor: What are the \u0001symptoms\u0002?",""]],"technology (n.)":[["guide-108-43","Organizers use modern \u0001technology\u0002 to provide an exciting light display in addition to hanging elaborate traditional lanterns.","主辦單位運用現代科技提供精彩的燈光秀,還掛上精緻的傳統燈籠。"],["leader-107-66","Software developers incorporate AI \u0001technology\u0002 into their products and use it to deal with the complicated job of big-data sorting and analysis.","軟體開發者把 AI 技術整合進產品,用來處理大數據分類與分析這種複雜工作。"]],"terminal (n.)":[["leader-112-42","Excuse me, which \u0001terminal\u0002 should I go to for the connecting flight to Chicago?","不好意思,轉機到芝加哥要去哪個航廈?"],["leader-106-14","A \u0001terminal\u0002 is an airport building that has all the facilities for passengers that are arriving or departing.","航廈是一棟機場建築,提供入境或離境旅客所需的一切設施。"]],"territory (n.)":[["guide-114-70","In international practice, most countries and \u0001territories\u0002 may refuse entry to a foreign visitor if their passport will expire less than six months after the date of arrival.","依國際慣例,若外國旅客的護照在抵達日後不到六個月就到期,多數國家與地區可能拒絕其入境。"],["guide-110-14","It is hard to predict the success of space travel since it is an unexplored \u0001territory\u0002.","太空旅行的成功難以預測,因為它是一個未探索的領域。"]],"tour (n.)":[["guide-110-28","\u0001Tour\u0002 guides' primary responsibility is to make sure the tour is safe for the group of tourists.","導遊的首要責任是確保旅程對整團遊客而言是安全的。"],["guide-109-54","A: Where does the \u0001tour\u0002 start off? B: At the main entrance.","A:導覽從哪裡出發? B:在正門口。"]],"traditional (adj.)":[["leader-115-10","This ancient city is a must-visit destination for every tourist to experience the \u0001traditional\u0002 culture and old town atmosphere.","這座古城是每位遊客必訪的目的地,可體驗傳統文化與老城氛圍。"],["leader-114-77","What makes the Odyssey different from \u0001traditional\u0002 cruise ships?","Odyssey 與傳統郵輪有何不同?"]],"transfer (v.)":[["leader-111-38","Guest: Please \u0001transfer\u0002 my call to an international operator.",""],["guide-109-38","Bamboo furniture is popular in Latin America as a result of bamboo-weaving craftsmanship \u0001transferred\u0002 from Taiwan.","竹製家具在拉丁美洲很受歡迎,這是源自台灣的竹編工藝傳入(移轉)的結果。"]],"trend (n.)":[["leader-114-14","Eco-friendly travel is now one of the fastest-growing \u0001trends\u0002 in the industry, and many people embrace this promising development.","環保旅遊現在是業界成長最快的趨勢之一,許多人擁抱這個有前景的發展。"],["leader-111-76","Safety & hygiene tourism \u0001trends\u0002 Whether it is airlines, cruises, hotels, restaurants or bars, since the outbreak of COVID-19, safety and hygiene standards have been absolutely paramount.","",4]],"trip (n.)":[["leader-112-38","Here is the itinerary for my \u0001trip\u0002 to Europe this coming summer. Do you have any suggestions?","這是我今夏歐洲之旅的行程表。你有什麼建議嗎?"],["leader-110-62","Cathy: How's your \u0001trip\u0002 in Japan, Jerry? Jerry: I really enjoyed it.","Cathy:Jerry,你的日本之旅如何? Jerry:我非常喜歡。"]],"unattended (adj.)":[["guide-115-1","When you are in public places, be sure not to leave your personal belongings \u0001unattended\u0002.","在公共場所,務必不要讓你的個人隨身物品無人看管。"],["guide-108-48","Beware of strangers at the airport and do not leave your personal items \u0001unattended\u0002.","在機場要提防陌生人,別讓私人物品無人看管。"]],"upgrade (v.)":[["leader-112-13","Some hotel loyalty programs award elite members \u0001upgrade\u0002 benefits after staying a certain number of nights.","有些飯店會員計畫在住滿一定晚數後,給予尊榮會員升等優惠。"],["guide-110-37","Can I \u0001upgrade\u0002 to business class?","我可以升等到商務艙嗎?"]],"urgent (adj.)":[["leader-114-10","Leaders of European Union countries arrived in Brussels for a summit, where migration is an \u0001urgent\u0002 topic.","歐盟各國領袖抵達布魯塞爾參加高峰會,移民是緊急議題。"],["leader-114-21","The global scientific community comes together and calls for immediate action on the \u0001urgent\u0002 global problem—air pollution.","全球科學界團結起來,呼籲對空氣污染這個緊急全球問題採取立即行動。"]],"utensil (n.)":[["leader-113-5","Customer: May I have two plastic forks, please? Receptionist: Unfortunately, we no longer provide any disposable \u0001utensils\u0002 due to the new environmental protection act.","顧客:可以給我兩支塑膠叉子嗎? 櫃台:抱歉,因新環保法我們不再提供任何拋棄式餐具。"],["leader-109-47","The customer looking at the forks and spoons complained about the dirty and stained \u0001utensils\u0002 to the waiter.","看著叉子湯匙的顧客,向服務生抱怨這些又髒又有污漬的餐具。"]],"vacancy (n.)":[["leader-112-49","Is there any \u0001vacancy\u0002 today?",""],["leader-108-14","Receptionist: ABC Hotel, may I help you? Justin: Do you have a \u0001vacancy\u0002 for a double room on March First?","櫃台:ABC 飯店,能為您服務嗎? Justin:3 月 1 日有空房的雙人房嗎?"]],"vacation (n.)":[["guide-111-13","The last thing you want on a \u0001vacation\u0002 is to find out hidden fees that you must pay.","度假時你最不想遇到的,就是發現隱藏的費用得付。"],["guide-109-18","We are on a tight budget, so we want to plan a \u0001vacation\u0002 that doesn't cost too much.","我們預算緊,所以想規劃一趟不太花錢的旅行。"]],"vandalism (n.)":[["leader-113-63","Singapore is famous for its strict laws. Anyone who is found guilty and convicted for \u0001vandalism\u0002 may face a fine or imprisonment.","新加坡以嚴格法律聞名。任何被判破壞公物罪成立者,可能面臨罰款或監禁。"],["guide-113-49","Parks and recreation staff received numerous calls over the weekend regarding \u0001vandalism\u0002 and damage at The Central Park.","週末公園與遊憩管理人員接到大量來電,反映中央公園的惡意破壞與損害。"]],"VAT":[["leader-112-62","A: Besides the discount, we can also keep the receipts to get a \u0001VAT\u0002 (value-added tax) refund at the airport. B: So great!","A:除了折扣,我們還能留著收據到機場辦加值稅退稅。 B:太棒了!"],["leader-111-56","Visitors to the EU may buy goods free of \u0001VAT\u0002 at the check-out. The clerk will ask you to show your passport and fill out a tax refund form.","到歐盟的遊客結帳時可買免加值稅商品。店員會請你出示護照並填一張退稅表。"]],"vehicle (n.)":[["guide-115-27","Renting a 1,500c.c. five-seater car allows for 48 hours of use. Before picking up the \u0001vehicle\u0002, please call the rental company to assist you in arranging the pickup.","租一輛 1,500c.c. 五人座車可使用 48 小時。取車前,請致電租車公司協助安排取車。"],["leader-110-23","Wearing seat belts is mandatory in all \u0001vehicles\u0002 for drivers globally.","全球所有車輛的駕駛都強制規定要繫安全帶。"]],"via (prep.)":[["leader-110-55","It's great that we can buy flight tickets \u0001via\u0002 both phone and internet without calling the travel agents. It saves us a lot of time.","我們能透過電話和網路買機票,不用打給旅行社,真好。這省了我們很多時間。"],["leader-106-79","What does the word \"\u0001via\u0002\" mean?","via 這個字是什麼意思?"]],"view (n.)":[["leader-112-57","Everyone can come to this corner. Based on my experience, it is the best \u0001view\u0002 to take a selfie or a group photo.","大家都可以到這個角落。以我經驗,這是拍自拍或團體照最佳的取景點。"],["leader-109-20","The \u0001view\u0002 outside the train was suddenly gone because it went through a(n) tunnel and it was dark outside.","火車窗外的景色突然消失,因為它穿過一個隧道,外面一片漆黑。"]],"wallet (n.)":[["leader-114-37","When was the last time you took out your \u0001wallet\u0002?",""],["leader-112-69","My \u0001wallet\u0002 was gone.",""]]};
